# BEGIN questbook (generated by tools/questbook/build_quests.py --lang; do not edit by hand)
betterquesting.questline.D4B4PFfzWT2Q4DUgPjN9oQ.name=GregGuns
betterquesting.questline.D4B4PFfzWT2Q4DUgPjN9oQ.desc=Guns that follow GregTech progression.
betterquesting.quest.4XzaW-3VWNKZOIlttBqwpQ.name=§8§lAdvanced Ammunition
betterquesting.quest.4XzaW-3VWNKZOIlttBqwpQ.desc=EV ammunition is made with titanium. Advanced Bullets (16 titanium foil, 16 titanium rounds and a TNT block make 16) fill Advanced Magazines, while 64 Rifle Bullets fill four Minigun Ammo Drums in one run. Both families have their own empty-magazine recipe in the EV press.%n%nEither an Advanced Magazine or a Minigun Ammo Drum counts. Hold eight magazines or four drums to finish this quest.%n%n[note]Only an EV press runs these recipes. Titanium plates and Mechanical Parts T3 are the gate inputs.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.8BwLq7VAWya-8GjMejFNKw.name=§2§lCases and Slugs
betterquesting.quest.8BwLq7VAWya-8GjMejFNKw.desc=Every loose round in the LV press is two small GregTech parts plus gunpowder. The case is a foil: a thin brass sheet made in the Bending Machine. The slug is a round: a small metal ball made in a Lathe from a nugget, or by hand with a file. Lead rounds go into pistol bullets and shotgun pellets; steel rounds go into rifle bullets.%n%nHold sixteen brass foils, sixteen lead rounds and sixteen steel rounds to finish. Each recipe takes sixteen of a part, so that is one run's worth of each. Brass is a copper and zinc alloy; check NEI for how to make it.%n%n[note]Make plenty. A single 9mm batch eats sixteen of each part.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.vzLd-yXoXoqAjpPwKjGgFQ.name=§5§lCharging at the Right Tier
betterquesting.quest.vzLd-yXoXoqAjpPwKjGgFQ.desc=A GregGuns electric item has one tier, and only a GregTech charger or battery buffer of exactly that tier will charge it. A higher-tier charger does not work, which is how GregTech treats its own tools. The Night Vision Goggles are MV, and the Tactical Mask is HV.%n%nHold either one to finish this quest, then match your charger to it. The pack's Battery Buffer and charger quests show how to build them.%n%n[note]The tooltip shows the charge but not the tier, so remember: goggles MV, mask HV. If it will not charge, you probably have the wrong tier of buffer.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.0I5k4WWbWyeGF7ZcFAjoiw.name=§2§lAmmo Depot
betterquesting.quest.0I5k4WWbWyeGF7ZcFAjoiw.desc=A stockpile is the sign of a working line. Fill a chest with two hundred and fifty-six 9mm bullets and sixty-four shotgun shells, so a fight never ends with an empty gun.%n%nKeep the stock in chests next to the press or in the Ammo Pouch from the Gear chapter. Guns look for ammo in the pouch first, then in your main inventory.%n%n[note]Sneak and right-click a loaded magazine to turn it back into loose stock.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.k0l8Z9XGUd2iHk_8CCjnOA.name=§6§lExplosives Handling
betterquesting.quest.k0l8Z9XGUd2iHk_8CCjnOA.desc=Grenade Launcher ammo is made in an MV Ammo Press: two aluminum plates, two TNT blocks and a gunpowder make eight 40mm grenades. Hold eight to finish this quest.%n%nExplosives want a separate room. Keep the TNT and gunpowder in a chest well away from the press, away from the furnace, and away from any creeper that could drift in.%n%n[warn]A chain explosion will empty your entire stockpile. Do not leave TNT lying next to the press.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.1fceSBv3UamtS9g-upePqA.name=§5§lFilling Bench (optional)
betterquesting.quest.1fceSBv3UamtS9g-upePqA.desc=An optional annex behind the packing end of the Works, built around six workbench tables. The bench takes finished rounds from the packing end and empty magazines from its own input bus, and puts loaded magazines in its own output bus, so the hall delivers finished magazines instead of loose rounds.%n%nHold eight AS50 or LMG magazines made by the Works to finish. The structure hologram shows the bench when you set its height channel to 1, and the Works scanner reports whether the bench is active.%n%n[note]The bench uses the same loaded-magazine recipes as the single presses.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.GvSjKY8wWcCuwQ_aNUAnQQ.name=§5§lFuel Tanks
betterquesting.quest.GvSjKY8wWcCuwQ_aNUAnQQ.desc=Fuel Tanks hold GregTech fuel for the Flamethrower and the Chainsaw. A GregTech Fluid Canner fills an empty tank with a thousand millibuckets of an accepted liquid fuel; Diesel from the oil line works. A full tank is worth a hundred rounds for the Flamethrower and three hundred for the Chainsaw.%n%nFill two Fuel Tanks to the brim and hold them to finish this quest; an empty or part-filled tank does not count. A gun only loads a completely full tank and hands the empty one back, so keep spares in rotation.%n%n[note]The tank itself is an HV Assembler recipe from stainless steel.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.FQ__DvIOXeyVzM3B16ZkhA.name=§5§lHeavy Rounds
betterquesting.quest.FQ__DvIOXeyVzM3B16ZkhA.desc=HV ammunition is a different class. High Caliber Rounds feed the AS50 anti-materiel rifle: eight brass casings, sixteen stainless steel rounds and four gunpowder make eight, in an HV Ammo Press. Rockets feed the Rocket Launcher: four stainless plates, two TNT, four gunpowder and an HV circuit make four.%n%nEither one completes this quest. Rounds this big are slow and expensive, so build up a stock before the fight, and check NEI for the exact inputs.%n%n[note]An HV press also runs every LV and MV recipe, faster.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.Nw-e_L32UOm4-we1yYkBlw.name=§2§lAmmo Logistics
betterquesting.quest.Nw-e_L32UOm4-we1yYkBlw.desc=A gun is only as good as its supply line. In GregGuns, ammunition is not crafted: it is produced, from GregTech parts, in a machine of its own. This chapter teaches that production line from the first brass foil to a multi-bay Ammunition Works, and it is why a big arsenal is a base project rather than a pocketful of lucky drops.%n%nThe plan: make the parts (foil cases and lead or steel slugs), press the three LV calibers in the Ammo Press, turn rounds into magazines, automate the line with item pipes, and stockpile. Later quests cover grenades, heavy rounds, charging electric gear, fuel tanks, and the Works that runs the whole thing in bulk.%n%nTo open the chapter, hold any LV round: sixteen 9mm or rifle bullets, or eight shotgun shells. If you finished the LV Ammo Press and 9mm quests, you already have them.%n%n[note]Ammo Press recipes have their own tab in NEI. Press U on a round to see where it is used.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.V7y4FFt1VQa-N8mwXKyomQ.name=§2§lMagazines in the Press
betterquesting.quest.V7y4FFt1VQa-N8mwXKyomQ.desc=Magazines are two press runs. The first makes eight empties from two steel plates, eight small steel springs and Mechanical Parts T2. The second fills them: four empties and twelve 9mm bullets make four loaded pistol magazines. One machine covers the whole chain.%n%nHold four empty and four loaded magazines to finish. For a quick single refill you can also craft an empty magazine with three bullets at a crafting table.%n%n[note]Sneak and right-click a loaded magazine to unload it, and the press can start over.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.6-1J9c-KUrSOvgJ5NR2PkQ.name=§2§lPipe It
betterquesting.quest.6-1J9c-KUrSOvgJ5NR2PkQ.desc=A press you feed by hand is a hobby. A press fed by item pipes is a factory. Run a pipe from a chest of parts to the press and another from its output to a second chest, with conveyor covers on the pipe ends to do the pulling. The press has room for six inputs and three outputs.%n%nLet the line run until it has made sixteen loaded pistol magazines. That is four filling runs, and it is the sort of job you do not want to babysit. The pack's Basic Transport: Items quest covers the pipe basics.%n%n[note]Pull rounds and empties from separate chests so a full output cannot starve the inputs.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.pijn8MOtV-ezyuZ1GzR0rg.name=§2§lRun the Press
betterquesting.quest.pijn8MOtV-ezyuZ1GzR0rg.desc=The LV Ammo Press makes three loose calibers, each from its own recipe: 9mm bullets (16 brass foil, 16 lead rounds and 2 gunpowder make 16), Shotgun Shells (8 brass foil, 24 lead rounds and 4 gunpowder make 8) and Rifle Bullets (16 brass foil, 16 steel rounds and 4 gunpowder make 16). The press picks the recipe from what you load, so no circuit is needed.%n%nRun one batch of each and hold all three. Ammo is slow by design, so scale up with more presses, higher tiers, or the Works later. 9mm feeds the pistol, revolver and SMGs, shells feed the shotguns, and rifle bullets feed the bolt rifle and the assault rifle and LMG magazines.%n%n[note]Every recipe shows in the press's NEI tab with its exact inputs.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.t09A1ZT-XI2ySLMI-VnX1Q.name=§5§lAmmunition Works
betterquesting.quest.t09A1ZT-XI2ySLMI-VnX1Q.desc=The Ammunition Works is a multiblock press hall with high parallels: four per press bay per voltage tier, so a long hall at HV runs dozens of presses' worth of work at once. Build it when one press cannot keep up. It is a 5-wide, 7-tall strip that grows three blocks per bay (two to eight bays).%n%nThe controller is an HV hand recipe with a Works Casing in each corner. The casings are stainless steel from an Assembler, each bay holds three Ram Housings, and an item pipe casing floor sets the belt tier. Each bay needs an interior lamp or the hall will not form. Use the structure hologram for the layout.%n%n[note]Parts go in at the feeder end and finished ammunition comes out of the packing end.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.lzzOUEnCU4q4ESs2ZOY_fg.name=§8§lAdvanced Ammunition
betterquesting.quest.lzzOUEnCU4q4ESs2ZOY_fg.desc=Advanced bullets are the EV ammo step up: titanium-jacketed rounds with a little TNT in the load. The PDW and the Pulse Rifle shoot them from Advanced Magazines.%n%nMake the bullets in an EV Ammo Press from titanium foil, titanium rounds and a block of TNT. Build empty Advanced Magazines, then load them in the same machine, four at a time with three advanced bullets each. NEI will tell you the circuit that selects each recipe.%n%nThis quest asks for a loaded magazine, so you know the whole line works.
betterquesting.quest.Ktu9FDk3W5-imEa0hwGXbQ.name=§8§lE. coli Culture
betterquesting.quest.Ktu9FDk3W5-imEa0hwGXbQ.desc=The Bio Gun runs on E. coli culture fluid, and the same fluid becomes a Plasma Membrane, a part you need for Cybernetic Parts. So this quest asks you to make the whole chain once and hand over the Cybernetic Parts.%n%nStart in the HV Bio Lab: an empty petri dish, a fermented spider eye and water make an E. coli dish. Put the dish in a BartWorks Bacterial Vat (EV) with Biomass and distilled water to grow culture fluid. An HV Centrifuge turns 1,000 mB of it into a Plasma Membrane.%n%nCraft Cybernetic Parts in the EV Assembler from fine electrum wire, EV circuits, plastic, redstone, soul sand and that membrane. Check NEI for the recipe.%n%n[note]You will fill the Bio Tank from the same fluid in the next quest.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.uj_5v9mYVEeKzFmxhDVdnw.name=§8§lBio Gun
betterquesting.quest.uj_5v9mYVEeKzFmxhDVdnw.desc=A gun that fires globs of biological culture. Its glob deals poison damage and leaves the target poisoned, unless the target wears full biological hazmat.%n%nBuild it in the EV Assembler from a Pump Mechanism, a Steel Receiver, a Plastic Gun Stock, a small titanium pipe, and titanium plates and screws. It comes out empty. Load a full Bio Tank and fire. The right button charges up for a stronger shot that costs more rounds.%n%n[note]Bio blobs on the ground need explosions.blockDamage enabled on the server. With it off, the glob still poisons targets but leaves no blobs.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.7V7dtADtUImcaUKp8HBOEQ.name=§8§lBio Tank
betterquesting.quest.7V7dtADtUImcaUKp8HBOEQ.desc=The Bio Tank is the ammo container for the Bio Gun. It holds 1,000 mB, and a full one is 30 rounds.%n%nBuild four tanks at a time in the EV Assembler from a titanium Large Fluid Cell, two titanium plates and two plastic plates. Then fill it with E. coli culture fluid in a GT Fluid Canner. If you need the fluid, the E. coli Culture quest tells you how.%n%n[note]The tank item is the same with or without fluid, so check the tooltip to see how full it is.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.0PJN6x7eXX2S4S6q_V2P4A.name=§8§lCarbon Gun Parts
betterquesting.quest.0PJN6x7eXX2S4S6q_V2P4A.desc=The pulse rifle, the PDW, the Tesla and Sonic rifles and every later energy weapon share three parts: a Carbon Barrel, a Carbon Receiver and a Carbon Gunstock. Build one of each and you can start on most of the tier.%n%nNone of them is true carbon: they are titanium with Epoxid Fiber Reinforced plates. The barrel uses a small titanium pipe and rings, the receiver is a hardened frame with titanium and epoxy plates, and the stock is epoxy and plastic with titanium screws. The Receiver also wants Mechanical Parts T3, made from titanium gears, springs and screws. NEI has all the numbers.%n%n[note]Mechanical Parts T3 are also needed by the Laser Rifle, the Exo Suit and the Anti Gravity Device, so make extras.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.D110ToiWWbqWJnwAqvAPTw.name=§8§lTesla or Sonic Rifle
betterquesting.quest.D110ToiWWbqWJnwAqvAPTw.desc=Two specialist energy weapons: the Tesla Rifle is built around an emitter coil, and the Sonic Rifle fires focused sound. Pick whichever suits the job.%n%nBoth run on a full EV battery hull and charge only in an EV charger or battery buffer. The Tesla Rifle uses an EV emitter as its coil. The Sonic Rifle uses a Sonic Emitter, which you build in the Assembler from an EV emitter, an electric piston and Mechanical Parts T3. Each also takes a Carbon Receiver and Gunstock.%n%n[note]An HV buffer will not accept an EV item. Make sure you have an EV charger first.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.0HC3BxJQWUui0NcJ3BI7vA.name=§8§lHazardous Environment Armor
betterquesting.quest.0HC3BxJQWUui0NcJ3BI7vA.desc=The HEV suit is built for places that want you dead. Worn as a full set, it protects against biological hazards, pollution gas and radiation, and it adds heat, cold and electrical protection while the chestplate holds a charge.%n%nEach piece is an EV Assembler recipe of Epoxid Fiber Reinforced and titanium plates and EV circuits. The chestplate is the electric part, charged in an EV charger or battery buffer. The quest wants the chestplate, but wear all four pieces: GT only counts the protection when the whole set has it.%n%n[note]Check NEI for the circuit number on each piece.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.knVvWsyhXNKqW5_Ifh1yBg.name=§8§lEnergy Weapons
betterquesting.quest.knVvWsyhXNKqW5_Ifh1yBg.desc=Titanium changes the game. EV brings lasers, pulse rifles, a drum-fed minigun, the Tesla and Sonic rifles, and armor that tells poison gas and radiation to keep out. Most of it is built from titanium and Epoxid Fiber Reinforced plates, so stock up before you start.%n%nEV recipes run in the EV Assembler at 1,920 EU/t. The energy weapons take a full battery hull and a dab of soldering alloy as part of their build, and they come out empty. A GregGuns electric item only charges in a GT charger or battery buffer of exactly its own tier, so an EV laser needs an EV buffer. An HV one will refuse it.%n%nAmmo steps up as well: advanced bullets and magazines for the pulse rifle, and ammo drums for the minigun. Start with the carbon parts, because most of this tier shares them.%n%n[note]Press R over any gun in NEI for the exact recipe. Quests only check what you carry and never take anything from you.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.tSdWXpg7WpWrfuyoRWiGOA.name=§8§lLaser Rifle
betterquesting.quest.tSdWXpg7WpWrfuyoRWiGOA.desc=No magazines, no brass, no reloading: the Laser Rifle runs on stored energy as long as you keep it charged. It is your first real energy weapon.%n%nBuild it in the EV Assembler from a Laser Barrel, a Hardened Receiver, a Plastic Gun Stock, Mechanical Parts T3, an EV circuit, a full EV battery hull and soldering alloy. It comes out uncharged, and you charge it in an EV charger or battery buffer. An HV buffer will not accept it.%n%n[note]The Laser Rifle is an IC2 electric item of tier 4. Check the tooltip for its charge.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.anUXm2cHVEy3w23fQVfW_g.name=§8§lLaser Focus
betterquesting.quest.anUXm2cHVEy3w23fQVfW_g.desc=The Laser Focus is the heart of every laser weapon: a ruby cut to a tight beam. Without it there is no Laser Barrel, and without a Laser Barrel there is no Laser Rifle.%n%nCut it in a GT Laser Engraver (EV) from a ruby and an EV emitter, with a white lens in the machine. The lens is not used up, but the emitter is. NEI shows the recipe if you press R on the focus.%n%n[note]A Laser Barrel is built later in the Assembler from the focus, a lens and electrum foil. Make a few at once.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.18GPEk2JVFif2NroFsHLXw.name=§8§lMinigun
betterquesting.quest.18GPEk2JVFif2NroFsHLXw.desc=A rotating-barrel wall of metal. The Minigun has an enormous rate of fire and burns through ammo just as fast, so bring a supply of drums.%n%nBuild it in the EV Assembler from six Hardened Steel Barrels, a Hardened Receiver, an EV electric motor, and titanium plates and screws. The motor spins the barrels. It is a ballistic gun, so it needs no charger. Its ammo drums are built empty, then filled with rifle bullets in the Ammo Press.%n%n[note]Hardened Receivers come from your HV days. If you have none, make some in the HV Assembler first.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.MxpCG_RiXvGv_cMybdc68w.name=§8§lPulse Rifle or PDW
betterquesting.quest.MxpCG_RiXvGv_cMybdc68w.desc=Two ballistic guns that eat advanced magazines. The Pulse Rifle adds a fire-control circuit to the build. The PDW is a compact personal defense weapon and needs no circuit. Build either one to move on.%n%nBoth are built in the EV Assembler from a Carbon Barrel, a Carbon Receiver and a Carbon Gunstock, plus titanium plates and screws. The Pulse Rifle adds a diamond lens, an EV circuit and soldering alloy; the PDW takes small titanium springs instead.%n%nNeither is an electric item, so they need no charger. The ammo is the work.
betterquesting.quest.ct79JLmwVza6IhVOWnSITg.name=§c§lSteam Armor
betterquesting.quest.ct79JLmwVza6IhVOWnSITg.desc=The Steam set is the best protection you can build without a single circuit: bronze plates over Tanned Leather, fourteen plates in all for the full set. The chestplate is the quest item (five plates and three Tanned Leather), and it is more than armor: it is a small steam engine.%n%nCarry coal or charcoal in your inventory and the chestplate burns it to power the set. Powered, the full set makes you faster, a little tougher and a better jumper. Without fuel it is still armor.%n%n[note]One piece of coal or charcoal refuels a quarter of a full charge. The chestplate only burns one when it has room for all of it, so nothing is wasted.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.Ijln77bBVEGQhTKU66-6Jg.name=§8§lEnergy Weapons Done
betterquesting.quest.Ijln77bBVEGQhTKU66-6Jg.desc=You made it through the electric age. A Laser Rifle in your hands and a Hazardous Environment suit on your back put you ahead of most of what EV can throw at you, including pollution gas, radiation and the occasional unfriendly creature.%n%nKeep your charger and your battery buffer close. Everything in this tier that uses energy needs a charger of exactly the right tier, and a flat laser is just an expensive club.%n%nIV is next, with tungstensteel, blasters, power armor and the anti-gravity device. The IV Assembler runs at 7,680 EU/t and the energy guns take a Lapotronic Orb for a battery, so start planning your power and your orbs.%n%n[note]This capstone pays extra, with three bags. Spend the coins at the Vending Machine.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.sRKOlCwmVseOIo_9jtROkQ.name=§8§lT3 Combat Armor
betterquesting.quest.sRKOlCwmVseOIo_9jtROkQ.desc=Advanced Combat armor resists armor-piercing hits better than any earlier set, and it needs no charge. It is the base for the Exo Suit later, so even if you plan to go powered, you want a set.%n%nEach piece is an EV Assembler recipe of Epoxid Fiber Reinforced and titanium plates, with a programmed circuit to pick the helmet, chestplate, leggings or boots. A chestplate is six epoxy plates and two titanium plates. The quest checks the chestplate, but wear the whole set for the bonuses.%n%n[note]Check NEI for the exact circuit numbers.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.08Lhb4uVX4Clef_DTgvKLw.name=§6§lGas Mask
betterquesting.quest.08Lhb4uVX4Clef_DTgvKLw.desc=The Gas Mask is a helmet-slot item that fully protects you from GregTech's gas hazard (the pollution effects of a polluted area) by itself, and it also cures poison and wither while its filter lasts. It must go in the helmet slot, not a Baubles slot, because GregTech only checks armor slots.%n%nBuild it in an MV assembler from five rubber plates, two glass panes, an aluminum plate and a Gas Mask Filter. When the filter runs out, combine the mask with a fresh filter in a crafting grid to refill it.%n%n[note]Gas is the hazard it stops. For radiation or heat you need a full armor set.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.OrL5XKPWWg6GJcQ_Lh3GEw.name=§5§lGlider
betterquesting.quest.OrL5XKPWWg6GJcQ_Lh3GEw.desc=The Glider lets you glide down from heights with no energy at all. It also goes in the wings slot, so choose between it and the Jump Pack.%n%nIt is assembled from a Glider Backpack and two Glider Wings, which come from Tanned Leather and stainless steel. Check NEI for the exact recipe.
betterquesting.quest.63bi8F0GU4qtylDedBiARA.name=§6§lKnow Your Hazards
betterquesting.quest.63bi8F0GU4qtylDedBiARA.desc=GregTech tracks hazards such as gas, radiation, heat, frost and electricity, and each protective item lists the ones it covers in its tooltip. Check the tooltip before you walk into a reactor hall.%n%nA full set protects when every piece does. T2 Commando armor covers electricity, Ranger Veteran armor covers radiation from its lead plating, and the Steam set covers heat. Bring one piece of any of these sets to practice reading its tooltip.%n%n[warn]One piece is not protection. Wear all four.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.sbT_rjFeWHivTHb6E8N5Pw.name=§2§lEquipment Slots
betterquesting.quest.sbT_rjFeWHivTHb6E8N5Pw.desc=Armor and gear sit in two places. Armor goes in the four armor slots, and so does the Gas Mask, because GregTech's hazard checks only read those slots. Galacticraft's oxygen gear uses Galacticraft's own slots. Everything else, goggles, back devices and the ammo pouch, goes in Baubles slots: head for goggles, wings for packs and gliders, quiver for the ammo pouch.%n%nPick up any starter chestplate to begin: Steam, Bandit (Scout) or Soldier's (T1 Combat). The Steam set is crafted by hand from bronze plates and Tanned Leather, and the T1 Combat set is built in an assembler. Check NEI for the exact pieces.%n%n[note]Wear every piece of a set for its full bonus. Items in Baubles slots drop when you die unless you keep your inventory.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.OeMwc2EdX3ybZ0eQTsRyKg.name=§5§lJump Pack
betterquesting.quest.OeMwc2EdX3ybZ0eQTsRyKg.desc=The Jump Pack is an electric back device for the wings slot. Each jump spends charge and gives you a boost, and it absorbs falls longer than three blocks, up to eight blocks for free, while it has charge. Only one back device fits the wings slot at a time.%n%nBuild it in an HV assembler: stainless steel plates and screws, a Glider Backpack, two Compressed Air Tanks, an Electric Piston and an HV circuit. Charge it in a GT charger before you leave.
betterquesting.quest.hsYHfI3wU3GvcuCf2VyPQQ.name=§6§lMedkit
betterquesting.quest.hsYHfI3wU3GvcuCf2VyPQQ.desc=The Medkit is the best healing item you can carry before the endgame. Use it below full health and, after 50 ticks of use, it heals you 6 health and gives Regeneration II for 20 seconds.%n%nIt is built in an MV assembler from two aluminum plates, four Bandages, a Redstone dust and 250 mB of ethanol. Bandages are the LV version of the same idea: a steel ring, three string and a slimeball make two. Check NEI.
betterquesting.quest.IDioba7CU1ORtYdr2qlldg.name=§6§lNight Vision Goggles
betterquesting.quest.IDioba7CU1ORtYdr2qlldg.desc=Night Vision Goggles go in the head Baubles slot, not the helmet slot, so you can wear them under a gas mask. They are electric, so charge them before you use them: they come out of the assembler empty.%n%nThey are built in an MV assembler from rubber plates, Tanned Leather, circuits, an MV Sensor, glass and an aluminum plate. Check NEI for the exact list.
betterquesting.quest.X79n0oWKWuCqQYwCYI0VPw.name=§5§lOxygen Mask and Tanks
betterquesting.quest.X79n0oWKWuCqQYwCYI0VPw.desc=For space and for bad air you need Galacticraft's oxygen gear. The Oxygen Mask goes in the mask slot and the Oxygen Tanks in the tank slots, because Galacticraft reads its own slots.%n%nThe Mask takes two plastic plates, two rubber plates and a stainless steel plate. The Tanks take four plastic plates, two Compressed Air Tanks and two stainless plates, and when they run dry, combine them with a Compressed Air Tank in a crafting grid to refill them. Check NEI.
betterquesting.quest.qT16OcFiXLahNbb0hFLu3A.name=§6§lAmmo Pouch
betterquesting.quest.qT16OcFiXLahNbb0hFLu3A.desc=The Ammo Pouch lives in the quiver Baubles slot and holds six stacks of ammunition with its own screen. When you reload, your guns look in the pouch before the rest of your inventory, so you stop digging through your bag in a fight.%n%nIt is a cheap MV assembler recipe: three Tanned Leather, two leather and an aluminum plate.
betterquesting.quest.n0jkztrIW--cq29iq3tU0g.name=§5§lAS50
betterquesting.quest.n0jkztrIW--cq29iq3tU0g.desc=The AS50 is an anti-materiel sniper rifle with a heavy zoom. It trades rate of fire for a hit that deletes most things at long range, and it makes quick work of armored targets.%n%nBuild it in the HV Assembler from two Hardened Steel Barrels, a Hardened Receiver, a Plastic Gun Stock, a diamond lens and stainless steel plates, screws and springs. Empty AS50 magazines are made first, then loaded with high caliber rounds in the Ammo Press.%n%nThe quest wants the rifle and one loaded magazine.
betterquesting.quest.YIoirIY4WpCQ1Ab-bNDp1w.name=§5§lFlamethrower
betterquesting.quest.YIoirIY4WpCQ1Ab-bNDp1w.desc=Fire is the cheapest damage per tank, and the Flamethrower sets fire to anything it touches. It is wonderful against crowds and nasty in a corridor.%n%nBuild it in the HV Assembler from a Pump Mechanism, an Iron Receiver, a Plastic Gun Stock, four Kanthal fine wires (the igniter coil), a small stainless steel pipe, and stainless steel plates and screws. A Fuel Tank is the ammo.%n%n[warn]It burns whatever it points at, and the target can be your ally. Mind who is in front of you.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.qt9hcjCwW3WF1ax0bz4saA.name=§5§lFuel Tank
betterquesting.quest.qt9hcjCwW3WF1ax0bz4saA.desc=The Fuel Tank is the ammo for two HV weapons, the Flamethrower and the Chainsaw. It holds 1,000 mB of fuel, and a Fluid Canner fills it for you.%n%nBuild four tanks at a time in the HV Assembler from a stainless steel Large Fluid Cell, two stainless steel plates and two rubber plates. The Large Fluid Cell is a GregTech item, so check NEI for it.%n%n[note]It takes diesel, gasoline, biodiesel or ethanol. A full tank is 100 flamethrower rounds or 300 chainsaw rounds.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.5lUh3JeXW82Mn5E5oL6xyA.name=§5§lGrenade Launcher
betterquesting.quest.5lUh3JeXW82Mn5E5oL6xyA.desc=The grenade launcher lobs the 40 mm grenades you learned to make at MV. It is the cheapest way to clear a room, and a good tool for a mob that keeps its distance.%n%nBuild it in the HV Assembler from a Hardened Steel Barrel, a Steel Receiver, a Plastic Gun Stock, and stainless steel plates, screws and springs. Press R over it in NEI for the full list. Grenades are the ammo, so carry a few.%n%n[note]Explosions hurt creatures, but on servers that keep the explosions.blockDamage setting off they leave the terrain alone.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.AITd0dNHXymupvIAd8gUNw.name=§5§lHigh Caliber Rounds
betterquesting.quest.AITd0dNHXymupvIAd8gUNw.desc=High caliber rounds are what the AS50 shoots: heavy brass-cased slugs that punch through armor. One of these rounds does more than a whole handful of rifle bullets.%n%nMake them in an HV Ammo Press from eight brass casings, sixteen stainless steel rounds and four gunpowder; a run gives you eight. NEI shows the recipe. Magazines are loaded with them in the same machine.%n%n[note]An AS50 magazine holds 10 rounds, filled from two high caliber rounds. A full stack goes a long way.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.5BKo8R81Uj6da0pd8scgsg.name=§5§lThe Infiltrator
betterquesting.quest.5BKo8R81Uj6da0pd8scgsg.desc=The Infiltrator is a suppressed M4. It plays a muffled shot sound instead of the M4's crack, which is easier on your ears and your neighbors.%n%nYou do not build it from scratch: put an M4 Assault Rifle in the HV Assembler with two stainless steel plates, two rubber plates, a long stainless steel rod and two glass lenses. The rubber and rod are the suppressor.%n%n[note]The M4 is used up, and the Infiltrator comes out fresh: its loaded rounds and camo skin do not carry over.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.LJaUhufHUVSDgcoU_8jGcw.name=§5§lHeavy Arms
betterquesting.quest.LJaUhufHUVSDgcoU_8jGcw.desc=Welcome to the heavy end of the arsenal. HV is where GregGuns grows teeth: belt-fed machine guns, anti-materiel rifles, rocket and grenade launchers, a flamethrower and two power tools that double as weapons. The gate material is stainless steel, so bring a few plates.%n%nEvery HV gun is built in an HV Assembler (480 EU/t) from stainless steel plates and screws, often with small springs, plus parts you already know from earlier tiers. The recipes get long, so press R over any gun in NEI and work backwards. The quests below start with shared components, then the guns that use them.%n%nAmmo moves up a tier as well. High caliber rounds, rockets and the fuel tank are HV work, made in the Ammo Press and the Assembler.%n%n[note]Quests only check that you are carrying the item. Nothing is ever taken from you, so keep your plates.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.jdNuu-ZwXCGTxyGIITt4oQ.name=§5§lLMG
betterquesting.quest.jdNuu-ZwXCGTxyGIITt4oQ.desc=The light machine gun is a belt-fed wall of lead. Its magazine holds 100 rounds, it has a mild zoom for steady fire at range, and it is the first gun where you really feel the difference between HV and MV firepower.%n%nBuild the LMG in the HV Assembler: a Hardened Steel Barrel, a Hardened Receiver, a Plastic Gun Stock, a glass lens, and stainless steel plates, screws and springs. Its magazines are an HV part too: build empty LMG Magazines, then load them with rifle bullets in the Ammo Press. The quest wants the gun and one loaded magazine.%n%n[note]One LMG magazine eats eight rifle bullets, so the rifle bullet line from MV is worth scaling up.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.MlsxQhL-X2GK38x-1ta9qQ.name=§5§lHardened Receiver
betterquesting.quest.MlsxQhL-X2GK38x-1ta9qQ.desc=The Hardened Receiver is the frame of every serious HV rifle. The SCAR, Vector, AS50, LMG and later the Minigun and Laser Rifle are all built around one, so make a few before you start on guns.%n%nCraft it in an HV Assembler from three stainless steel plates, two stainless steel screws and a Mechanical Parts T2. Press R on the receiver in NEI for the exact recipe.%n%n[note]The AUG takes the plainer Steel Receiver instead, so it is the one rifle you can build without this part.[/note]
betterquesting.quest._-zv3UWTW46bCXsTCjRQmA.name=§5§lAUG, SCAR or Vector
betterquesting.quest._-zv3UWTW46bCXsTCjRQmA.desc=Three specialist rifles, one quest: build any of them to move on. The AUG is the all-rounder with a good scope, the SCAR is the precise one with its diamond lens, and the Vector is a fast-firing SMG for close work.%n%nAll three come from the HV Assembler. Each takes a Hardened Steel Barrel, a Plastic Gun Stock, a lens (two glass lenses for the AUG, one for the Vector, a diamond lens for the SCAR) and stainless steel plates, screws and springs. The SCAR and Vector use the Hardened Receiver; the AUG uses a Steel Receiver. Check NEI for the exact list.%n%nThe AUG and SCAR load Assault Rifle Magazines. The Vector takes SMG Magazines.
betterquesting.quest.ezPElBIkVpi1ldbBKRj5Gw.name=§5§lRockets
betterquesting.quest.ezPElBIkVpi1ldbBKRj5Gw.desc=Rockets are the biggest bang you can carry at HV: a real blast radius in a single shot. The Rocket Launcher fires them, and so does the Grim Reaper much later.%n%nMake them in the HV Ammo Press from four stainless steel plates, two TNT, four gunpowder and an HV circuit that acts as the fuze. Each run yields four rockets. NEI will show the exact recipe.%n%n[warn]Rockets blow up where they land. Never fire one at a wall closer than the blast radius, and never at your own feet.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.2xo9O6LeXQG5oYfZak5APA.name=§5§lRocket Launcher
betterquesting.quest.2xo9O6LeXQG5oYfZak5APA.desc=A shoulder-fired launcher for the moments when a grenade is not enough. It comes empty, so every rocket you fire comes from your own stock.%n%nBuild it in the HV Assembler from two Hardened Steel Barrels, a Steel Receiver, a small stainless steel pipe, and stainless steel plates and screws. NEI has the full recipe.%n%nKeep your distance: the blast radius is real, and a rocket at point-blank range will hurt you too.%n%n[note]With explosions.blockDamage off, a default server keeps its terrain safe. Creatures still take the full hit.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.bcXXo-9EW4ilXvMTgUopuA.name=§5§lHeavy Arms Done
betterquesting.quest.bcXXo-9EW4ilXvMTgUopuA.desc=That is the heavy tier. You hold a belt-fed LMG, a sniper that takes things apart at range, and a launcher that can level a room. With these three you can walk into most of the pack's HV hazards and come out the other side.%n%nThe next step is energy. EV swaps brass and powder for batteries and lenses: laser rifles, pulse rifles and electric armor, all built from titanium. The EV Assembler runs at 1,920 EU/t, and those guns only charge at an EV charger or battery buffer, so plan your power before you start.%n%nThis quest pays double, so spend the coins at the Vending Machine and open the bag when you are ready.%n%n[note]Bring your Hardened Receivers forward. The Laser Rifle and the Minigun use them too.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.IDtZWJGBXVmSPjlEoYvouA.name=§5§lChainsaw and Power Hammer
betterquesting.quest.IDtZWJGBXVmSPjlEoYvouA.desc=Two tools that happen to be weapons. The Chainsaw is a fuel-hungry melee weapon whose right click also fires a short ranged cut. The Power Hammer charges a shockwave that hits everything and breaks blocks in a small cube in front of you.%n%nThe Chainsaw takes a Fuel Tank. The Power Hammer takes a Compressed Air Tank, a sibling of the Fuel Tank built from an aluminum Large Fluid Cell. Both are HV Assembler builds around an Iron Receiver, an HV Electric Piston and stainless steel plates and screws, and both come unloaded. Check NEI for either recipe and build whichever you like.%n%n[note]Hold right click to charge the hammer: the longer the charge, the more air it spends and the harder it hits.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.hw_7QfMgWvSvEBdcM5sh4g.name=§5§lAir-Defense Battery
betterquesting.quest.hw_7QfMgWvSvEBdcM5sh4g.desc=A radar tells you a missile is coming; the Air-Defense Battery does something about it. It holds 4 stacks of 16 SAMs and a data stick.%n%nPut a stick that carries a radar's link in its slot and it fires by itself at the nearest threat that radar reports within 256 blocks: one SAM a second at most, 400 EU each. A SAM does 40 damage, so Tier 1 and Tier 2 missiles fall to one and a Tier 3 missile takes two. Check NEI for both recipes. Make a battery and a SAM.%n%n[warn]The warhead goes off where the missile is hit, so shoot early, well away from your base.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.RZXbB-HhX26yt8B7h7KA5Q.name=§5§lCompressed Steel Airframe
betterquesting.quest.RZXbB-HhX26yt8B7h7KA5Q.desc=The missile's airframe is a column of three compressed steel plates, the same Galacticraft plates the rocket program uses.%n%nCompressed plates come from the Implosion Compressor: a steel plate plus an explosive charge. Check NEI for the charge it takes. Make three; the body page has exactly three plate slots in one vertical column.
betterquesting.quest.pQH3ygqDU3-7Whg8HZmspw.name=§5§lAntidote
betterquesting.quest.pQH3ygqDU3-7Whg8HZmspw.desc=The Antidote is a syringe for the bad days. The Assembler makes 2 at HV from a rubber plate, a stainless steel plate and 2 charcoal dust. Check NEI.%n%nHold use for 1.6 seconds and it cures poison, hunger, weakness, slowness, nausea, mining fatigue and radiation at once, then guards you against them for 3 minutes. Armor still has to keep the cause off, and it does nothing against fire or explosions. Make one.
betterquesting.quest.1b4KK5qOVnCDZaz5lkRppw.name=§d§lAnti-Gravitational Warhead
betterquesting.quest.1b4KK5qOVnCDZaz5lkRppw.desc=The other exotic Tier 3 warhead takes the anti-gravitational payload, fitted to an Inert T3 Warhead in the Assembler at LuV (2 LuV Field Generators and 4 Nether Stars), then up to 64 Plastic Explosive charges. Check NEI.%n%nFor 30 seconds it lifts up to 512 plain blocks within 20 blocks off the ground, top layer first, and floats the living things there. Machines and chests stay put, and every lifted block lands again or drops as an item. Make one.%n%n[warn]What goes up comes down. Anything floating when the effect ends falls.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.b7WClCi0VriyYrcPwpkG5g.name=§2§l§nAntimatter
betterquesting.quest.b7WClCi0VriyYrcPwpkG5g.desc=Antimatter is the Tier 4 casing: naquadria plates, two blocks tall, up to 128 charges. The Assembler makes the Inert T4 Warhead at UV from 8 naquadria plates, a Fuze Assembly Mk III, a Heavy Duty Nose Cone Tier 3, 12 Heavy Duty Plates Tier 6, a UV Sensor, a UV Emitter and 2 UV circuits, fits the antimatter payload at UV (2 UV Field Generators, a Quantum Eye and 4 plutonium-241 ingots), and fills it with 128 Plastic Explosive. Check NEI.%n%nA full warhead blasts 80 blocks, and nothing living in the inner 48 survives, bosses included. It leaves no fallout, and it ends any Red Matter within 200 blocks. The Tier 3 missile carries it from the silo. Make one.%n%n[warn]Bosses are not safe and neither are you. Launch it from far away.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.jnrSZsr_XfOI0sMCPeYxUQ.name=§d§lTier 3 on the Assembly Line
betterquesting.quest.jnrSZsr_XfOI0sMCPeYxUQ.desc=The Tier 3 missile is the big one: six blocks tall, 8,000 mB of rocket fuel, 20 to 8,000 blocks of range (10,000 from a silo), and the only body that carries the heaviest casings, antimatter and red matter included. It launches only from a Missile Silo with a LuV Energy Hatch.%n%nBuild the first one by hand. The Tier 3 chip comes from the Circuit Assembler at LuV (a Multifiberglass board, 2 Master circuits and 8 fine platinum wires) and is engraved with a yellow lens. The NASA Workbench page takes the Tier 4 rocket's hull, fins and engine (four Heavy Duty Plates Tier 4, four Heavy Rocket Fins and a Heavy Rocket Engine) and a Guidance Computer Mk III, which fits but gives no guidance steps on a body this heavy.%n%nThis is the one missile body built on GregTech's §lAssembly Line§r. Scan a hand-built Missile Body T3 onto a data stick in the Scanner (180 seconds at LuV) to unlock the recipe. The line then builds it from the same plates, fins and engine, 2 Master circuits and 250 L of lubricant in 60 seconds at LuV. Check NEI. Build two Tier 3 bodies.%n%n[note]Keep one hand-built body aside for the scan. The Tier 1 and Tier 2 bodies never need the Assembly Line: the Assembler builds those.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.kbVxkPNqV8-lYmEtAdnFnQ.name=§5§lMissile Body
betterquesting.quest.kbVxkPNqV8-lYmEtAdnFnQ.desc=Time to put the airframe together. With the Missile Schematic T1 slotted, the NASA Workbench's missile page shows the slots on a rocket outline: three compressed steel plates down the middle, four fins at the bottom, the engine at the base and the guidance computer beside the nose.%n%nFill every slot and take the Missile Body T1 from the result slot. It uses one item from each slot. There is no warhead slot: the warhead goes on the body later, on the launch pad. A Tier 1 body flies 20 to 1,000 blocks and needs 2,000 mB of fuel.%n%nHand-building comes first, and it never stops working. Once the parts flow, your HV Assembler builds the same body without the workbench: see [quest]Automate the Body[/quest].
betterquesting.quest.U6dESff0WcWrDcNsiMIhbg.name=§5§lAutomate the Body
betterquesting.quest.U6dESff0WcWrDcNsiMIhbg.desc=One missile is a demonstration. Twenty is a policy. The NASA Workbench is fine for your first body, but filling slots by hand gets old fast, so let a GregTech machine do it: your plain §lHV Assembler§r builds Missile Bodies with no research and no data stick.%n%nThe Assembler takes the same parts as the workbench page: three compressed steel plates, four Tier 1 rocket fins and a Tier 1 rocket engine. In place of the guidance computer it wires in 2 Advanced circuits, and it wants 250 L of lubricant in its fluid slot. A Tier 1 body takes 30 seconds at HV. The Tier 2 body works the same way in an EV Assembler: four compressed titanium plates, Heavy Rocket Fins and Engine, 2 Data circuits, the same lubricant, 45 seconds. Check NEI.%n%nA machine-built body has no guidance steps. To make it land closer, put the body and a better Guidance Computer back in the Assembler: 15 seconds at the body's voltage, and the same body comes out guided. Build four Tier 1 bodies.%n%n[note]The Tier 1 body needs HV power, so an LV or MV Assembler won't run it, and a Tier 2 body needs an EV one.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.zzEDTkwIUhOA1pmQn_LzMg.name=Trigger: Missile Body Skip
betterquesting.quest.zzEDTkwIUhOA1pmQn_LzMg.desc=No Description
betterquesting.quest.QkAbf_buVzC3oKgieSuXag.name=§5§lPlastic Explosive
betterquesting.quest.QkAbf_buVzC3oKgieSuXag.desc=Every warhead's explosive is Plastic Explosive: one piece is one charge. More charges make a wider, harder blast, though each extra charge adds a little less than the one before.%n%nThe Assembler makes 4 at HV from 2 PTFE plates and 2 Industrial TNT. Check NEI. That's the only place Industrial TNT goes; a warhead takes the charges and nothing else explosive.%n%nMake five, enough to fill a Tier 1 casing. Heavier casings hold 20, 64 and finally 128, so it's worth automating early.%n%n[warn]Plastic Explosive is safe in a chest. Once it's loaded into a warhead it isn't.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.4KjNfDUmXW28JarHt0SHGA.name=§5§lMissile Chip
betterquesting.quest.4KjNfDUmXW28JarHt0SHGA.desc=Every missile starts as a chip. The Missile Chip T1 holds the flight program, and it's the first thing the NASA Workbench will ask about.%n%nMake it in the GregTech Circuit Assembler at HV (20 seconds) from a Plastic Circuit Board, 2 Advanced circuits and 4 fine gold wires. Check NEI for the exact recipe. The chip is only half the job: the next quest engraves it into a schematic.
betterquesting.quest.I9JCb4IjWZ-4KPHIS_CDlA.name=§5§lLaunch Control
betterquesting.quest.I9JCb4IjWZ-4KPHIS_CDlA.desc=The Launch Control is the button. It's a GregTech single block at HV, made in the Assembler from an HV machine hull, an HV sensor, an HV emitter, an empty data stick and 2 Advanced circuits. Check NEI.%n%nSet it against one edge of the pad, level with it (corners don't count, the way Galacticraft's own launch controller attaches) and power it at HV. Get a target with a Radar Gun: aim it at the spot, then right-click the Launch Control with it, or drop the gun in the slot and press Load target. You can also type the target X and Z or press Use My Position. The screen shows the range (at least 20 blocks, at most 1,000 for Tier 1) and the blast radius to expect.
betterquesting.quest.zbtOc1iKW_GtMQQ-1g55zg.name=§5§lDe-arming
betterquesting.quest.zbtOc1iKW_GtMQQ-1g55zg.desc=Built the wrong warhead, or want the parts back? Every step of the chain runs backwards. Put a live warhead and a Defuse Kit in a crafting grid: each craft takes out up to 8 Plastic Explosive, whole, for one use of the kit. The last charge out leaves the inert warhead with its payload, ready for a different load.%n%nThe Cutting Machine does the rest at the warhead's own tier: it empties a full warhead in one go, takes a payload out and cuts a bare casing back into its plates, Fuze Assembly, nose cone and hull plates; its sensor, emitter and circuits are spent. Check NEI.%n%nUnload a T1 warhead until only the inert casing is left.%n%n[note]A payload's parts come back, but any fluid it held is spent. A Macerator or Arc Furnace only gives back a warhead's metal.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.rQaB9lE6UTKiPd5-PZNH4Q.name=§5§lDemolition Charge
betterquesting.quest.rQaB9lE6UTKiPd5-PZNH4Q.desc=A warhead doesn't need a missile. Place it where you want the hole and light it with Flint and Steel, a Fire Charge or a redstone pulse. The fuse is 3 seconds plus 1 second per 3 blocks of blast radius, so a full Condensed warhead gives you 6 seconds to leave.%n%nFill a Condensed warhead to its cap of 5 charges for the biggest hole a Tier 1 casing makes: in a crafting grid, or all at once in the Assembler from a bare Inert T1 Warhead and 5 Plastic Explosive on circuit 1. Keep a lighter with it.%n%n[warn]Get well clear, and keep other charges away: another explosion sets a warhead off in half a second.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.4iGni58RWjWEJwmVI20ehw.name=§8§lEMP Tower
betterquesting.quest.4iGni58RWjWEJwmVI20ehw.desc=The EMP Tower sends one pulse when you press Fire, on a redstone rising edge or from a computer. You pick the radius, 4 to 100 blocks, and the pulse costs 25 EU per square block of radius: 90,000 EU at 60. It's an EV Assembler recipe; check NEI.%n%nThe pulse drains the 64 nearest machines, batteries and Battery Buffers to zero and gives each multiblock one maintenance issue. A missile in range is destroyed 50 percent of the time, has its guidance fried 40 percent of the time and has its warhead set off 1 percent of the time.%n%n[warn]The pulse doesn't care whose machines it drains. Keep the tower away from your own base.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.2yILNJN9XD-syccitlHmRw.name=§5§lRocket Engine
betterquesting.quest.2yILNJN9XD-syccitlHmRw.desc=The Tier 1 missile burns the same engine as the Galacticraft Tier 1 rocket. It's the priciest single part of the body, so take your time with it.%n%nThe pack's engine recipe uses SDHD120 and heavy-duty plates, a fuel canister, a firebox casing and a detector. Check NEI for the current recipe. One engine per body.
betterquesting.quest.U_A7n-StWs2usSzdLJCy0w.name=§d§lEnder Warhead
betterquesting.quest.U_A7n-StWs2usSzdLJCy0w.desc=The Ender warhead is a Tier 3 casing. Fit the ender payload to an Inert T3 Warhead in the Assembler at LuV (a LuV Emitter and 16 Eyes of Ender), then load up to 64 Plastic Explosive charges. Check NEI.%n%nIt digs no crater. For 8 seconds it pulls every living thing within 24 blocks toward the center, and anything that reaches the middle (within 4 blocks) is sent to one landing spot 40 to 128 blocks away, up to 64 per blast. Bosses are pulled but never sent. It flies only from the silo. Make one.%n%n[warn]The landing spot is random. Don't stand in the pull unless you want to go too.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.nMkORPpQW06myC5nS9Hs9g.name=§b§lFallout Cleanup
betterquesting.quest.nMkORPpQW06myC5nS9Hs9g.desc=A nuclear blast leaves irradiated earth, hot earth near ground zero, trinitite and a little fallout goo. Mine it out in full hazmat armor.%n%nTrinitite Shards are macerated at HV into Crushed Trinitite, which a Centrifuge at HV turns into dusts. Goo is dissolved in 1,000 L of nitric acid in a Chemical Reactor at LuV, then centrifuged at EV. While goo stands in a chunk its ground never heals, so dig it up. Make Crushed Trinitite.%n%n[warn]Irradiated ground hurts without full hazmat armor.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.jXQXfz3gV6yHJTC4CPvxqw.name=§5§lRocket Fins
betterquesting.quest.jXQXfz3gV6yHJTC4CPvxqw.desc=A missile is a rocket that doesn't come back, so it flies on rocket fins. The body takes four Galacticraft Tier 1 Rocket Fins, one in each fin slot, the same fins the Tier 1 rocket uses.%n%nIn this pack the fins are made from compressed steel and heavy-duty plates. Check NEI, or the [quest]Space Race[/quest] tab, which walks the rocket parts too.
betterquesting.quest.jCjcKUqDWJezjQmc98WtTw.name=§5§lFuel the Missile
betterquesting.quest.jCjcKUqDWJezjQmc98WtTw.desc=The missile's tank starts empty and only fills while it stands on the pad. Attach a Galacticraft Fuel Loader to the pad and feed it rocket fuel.%n%nA Tier 1 missile takes 2,000 mB of Cetane-Boosted Diesel or RP-1, or a better rocket fuel; plain Galacticraft fuel is refused. It won't launch until the tank is full. Fuel left unburned at impact makes the blast up to 25 percent wider, so a close target hits harder than a far one.
betterquesting.quest.yp9NwUmoWfe2f_vUg_3yWQ.name=§5§lFuze Assembly
betterquesting.quest.yp9NwUmoWfe2f_vUg_3yWQ.desc=Every Tier 1 warhead starts as an inert casing, and a Fuze Assembly Mk I is built into it: the timer and trigger that make the charges go off when and where you want, and nothing before that.%n%nIt's an Assembler recipe at HV from an Advanced circuit, a steel plate and 4 fine copper wires, the same shopping list as the Guidance Computer. Check NEI. Make a few: every Inert T1 Warhead takes one, and so do the HV launcher warheads.
betterquesting.quest.u-IyESjmUWCDcvAt2GDrTA.name=§5§lGolden Dome
betterquesting.quest.u-IyESjmUWCDcvAt2GDrTA.desc=Prefer a computer at the controls? The Golden Dome is a yellow OpenComputers floppy with ready-made programs, made in the Assembler at HV from a blank floppy and a Good circuit. Check NEI.%n%nPut it in a computer's disk drive and link your machines through an OpenComputers Adapter. The launch program fires a missile (it always asks first), radarwatch lists radar contacts with an alarm, autodefense fires your batteries at incoming missiles, and emp runs the EMP tower. Build an Adapter to wire it up.
betterquesting.quest.-5Jq5qRwVCiCGJdVh_AtOA.name=§5§lGuidance Computer
betterquesting.quest.-5Jq5qRwVCiCGJdVh_AtOA.desc=The Guidance Computer tells the missile where to come down. The Mk I is the base computer for a Tier 1 body; better computers land closer.%n%nMake the Mk I in the Assembler at HV from an Advanced circuit, a steel plate and 4 fine copper wires. A Mk II (EV) gives a Tier 1 body one step of guidance and a Mk III (IV) two, so the missile scatters less. You can fit a better computer into a finished body later in the Assembler. Check NEI.
betterquesting.quest.TB8tfZEMWJ67-7Wz1ovSCA.name=§5§lHandheld Tools
betterquesting.quest.TB8tfZEMWJ67-7Wz1ovSCA.desc=Three tools for the field. The Radar Gun aims 200 blocks and stores that spot as a target; right-click a Launch Control to copy it in, or drop the gun in the Launch Control's slot and press Load target. The Remote Detonator links to a placed warhead when you sneak-click it, and a right-click lights its fuse from 128 blocks (HV), 256 (EV) or 512 (IV).%n%nThe Defuse Kit puts a lit fuse out (right-click), or takes apart a missile standing on a pad or in a silo (left-click) before its countdown starts; it lasts 32 uses. Check NEI for the recipes. Make all three.%n%n[warn]A lit fuse doesn't wait for you. Defuse fast or run.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.N3HXrk3xVV-GngmeU1_afg.name=§5§lInert Warhead
betterquesting.quest.N3HXrk3xVV-GngmeU1_afg.desc=A warhead is built in steps, and the first is an empty one. The Inert T1 Warhead is the missile's nose: a Tier 1 rocket's nose cone and hull plating around a stainless steel casing, with a Fuze Assembly Mk I and the arming electronics wired into it. There is no explosive inside yet, so it is perfectly safe: it can't be placed, launched or set off, and a silo won't take it.%n%nThe Assembler makes it at HV, on programmed circuit 2, from 4 stainless steel plates, a Fuze Assembly Mk I, a Nose Cone, 12 Heavy Duty Plates, an HV Sensor, an HV Emitter and 2 Advanced circuits. Check NEI. The warhead is the expensive part of a missile. Every heavier casing follows the same pattern at its own tier, with that tier's rocket nose cone and hull: titanium and a Mk II fuze at EV, then tungstensteel, naquadria and neutronium with a Mk III.%n%nFrom here you customize it. Fit a payload in the Assembler if you want a special blast, then load Plastic Explosive charges to make it live. A Tier 1 casing takes up to 5 charges.%n%n[note]An inert warhead looks like the real thing, only darker. Read the tooltip: it shows the payload and Charges: 0.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.nxM388UCWdaf6Sw2mgje9A.name=§5§lMissile Materials
betterquesting.quest.nxM388UCWdaf6Sw2mgje9A.desc=So you want to throw a bomb at something a thousand blocks away. Welcome to the ICBM program. A GregGuns missile is not one crafting recipe: it's a §lMissile Body§r and a §lWarhead§r, built separately from GregTech parts and Galacticraft rocket hardware, then stacked on a launch pad and fired from a Launch Control.%n%nThis chapter walks the Tier 1 build part by part, the way the [quest]Space Race[/quest] tab walks the Tier 1 rocket. Start by stocking the materials almost every part shares. Advanced circuits go into the Missile Chip (2), the Guidance Computer (1), the Fuze Assembly (1) and the Launch Control (2). Stainless steel plates are the warhead casing, and steel plates go into the computer and the fuze. Nothing in the ICBM program runs below HV, so your HV Assembler and Circuit Assembler will be busy.%n%nThen work through the part quests below: chip and schematic, compressed plates, fins, engine and guidance for the body, a fuze for the warhead. Check NEI on every part.%n%n[note]The ICBM chapter needs Galacticraft and the ICBM module (config modules.icbm). If you already hold a finished Missile Body T1, the body's part quests complete themselves.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.Y2gOH5_qWrOdflkhB64vCg.name=§5§lFirst Launch
betterquesting.quest.Y2gOH5_qWrOdflkhB64vCg.desc=Everything comes together here: a Missile Body, a warhead and a Launch Control, with the pad and the fuel loader you already built. Hold all three to finish the quest, then go and fire it.%n%nStack the missile on the pad, arm it, fill the tank and set a target. Press Launch, or give the Launch Control a redstone pulse. A 10-second countdown starts, and Abort still stands the missile down, armed and fueled. After ignition there's no turning back: the missile climbs, flies its arc and detonates on impact. A Tier 1 flight at full range takes about a minute. The pad, the fuel loader and the Launch Control come through unharmed.%n%nNext: a Tier 2 missile, radar and air defense, and the Missile Silo.%n%n[warn]Make sure nobody stands at the target, you included. A missile that is shot down still goes off where it is hit.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.rXAr4sE_X9KKmD7KlJSsBQ.name=§5§lLauncher Warhead
betterquesting.quest.rXAr4sE_X9KKmD7KlJSsBQ.desc=Your shoulder launchers can carry a blast type too. A Launcher Warhead is a small charge: High Explosive, Heavy Slug, Incendiary and Phosphorus at HV and Demolition at EV for the Rocket Launcher and Grim Reaper; Grenade HE (HV) and Grenade Cluster (EV) for the Grenade Launcher; EMP (LuV) for the Nuke Launcher.%n%nCraft it with the launcher in the crafting grid for 4 charges, up to 16. Each shot spends one charge and the launcher's own round, and goes off as a small blast; its center damage is capped at 1.25 times the launcher's own. Make a High Explosive one; check NEI for its recipe.%n%n[warn]Keep your distance from the impact point: these rounds hurt you as much as your target.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.oXlfsvjaVNmda25AXg-SwQ.name=§b§lNuclear Warhead
betterquesting.quest.oXlfsvjaVNmda25AXg-SwQ.desc=The nuclear warhead is a Tier 3 casing, two blocks tall. Start with an Inert T3 Warhead (the Assembler at LuV: 8 tungstensteel plates, a Fuze Assembly Mk III, a Heavy Nose Cone, 12 Heavy Duty Plates Tier 4, a LuV Sensor, a LuV Emitter and 2 Master circuits), fit the nuclear payload at ZPM (8 uranium-235 ingots, 4 plutonium ingots and 2 ZPM Field Generators to hold the core), then load 64 Plastic Explosive, its implosion lens. It flies only on a Tier 3 missile, from the silo. Check NEI.%n%nA full warhead blasts 64 blocks, and nothing living inside the inner 60 percent (38 blocks at full fill) survives, bosses included. The top layer of ground is left irradiated for about an hour.%n%n[warn]Cross the blast zone only in full hazmat armor, and stand well back from the launch target. There is no safe distance inside the inner radius.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.4TbIziOkWxSMv8pMnJE2dA.name=§5§lLaunch Pad
betterquesting.quest.4TbIziOkWxSMv8pMnJE2dA.desc=A missile launches from a Galacticraft launch pad: nine pad blocks in a 3 by 3 square. You may already have one from the rocket program.%n%nRight-click the pad with the body; whichever pad block you click, it stands in the middle. Then place the warhead on its nose, where it seats flush. Sneak and right-click the body with an empty hand to arm it, which turns the stack into one missile. A warhead heavier than the body's tier is refused at arming.%n%n[note]Changed your mind? Sneak and right-click the armed missile with an empty hand: it drops the body and the warhead, and the fuel is lost.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.lP7P2SnQV5OkH_xCiZG1lQ.name=§5§lChoose a Payload
betterquesting.quest.lP7P2SnQV5OkH_xCiZG1lQ.desc=A plain warhead just goes bang. A payload changes what the bang does: steel fragments, a lead mass, napalm, a dizzying or choking gas, smoke, or a field generator that pushes everything away or pulls it in.%n%nThe Assembler fits a payload at HV: put one bare Inert T1 Warhead in with the payload's parts and the right programmed circuit, and you get the same inert warhead with that payload, ready for charges. The Shrapnel payload, for example, is one Steel Fragmentation Sleeve. Check NEI for every payload and its circuit.%n%n[note]A payload holds no explosive. You still load Plastic Explosive afterward. Fitting a new payload to a casing that already has one replaces the old payload.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.70Tzn2miVgKdpAJQSq449g.name=§5§lRadar
betterquesting.quest.70Tzn2miVgKdpAJQSq449g.desc=Other people have missiles too. A radar watches every missile in flight and flags the ones that will land inside its protected radius, which you set on its screen (64 blocks to begin with).%n%nThe radar is a small 3 by 3 build of Radar Casing, two high, with one casing on top for the dish. The Assembler makes the casing four at a time at HV from 6 stainless steel plates. The HV controller sees 128 blocks and the EV controller 256, at any height; put an Energy Hatch of its tier and a Maintenance Hatch in the base. Its redstone output on every side is the number of incoming missiles, up to 15. Right-click the controller with a data stick to save its link for a battery. Build a radar.
betterquesting.quest.Xmv-nEDuUGOM661dF3bKgg.name=§9§lRadar Tower
betterquesting.quest.Xmv-nEDuUGOM661dF3bKgg.desc=When 256 blocks isn't enough warning, build the Radar Tower: a 3 by 3 tower of Radar Casing, 7 blocks tall, with a Gantry Beam mast up the middle and a dish turning on top.%n%nIts range comes from its weakest Energy Hatch: 512 blocks at IV, 768 at LuV, 1,024 at ZPM, 1,280 at UV and 1,536 at UHV. Put an Energy Hatch and a Maintenance Hatch in the bottom ring, and set the protected radius from the R button on the controller screen. Build the controller; check NEI.
betterquesting.quest.qVqk5gj-XKK1KCOeW5QUyQ.name=§4§l§nRed Matter
betterquesting.quest.qVqk5gj-XKK1KCOeW5QUyQ.desc=Red Matter is the Tier 5 casing and the end of the line. The Assembler makes the Inert T5 Warhead at UHV from 8 neutronium plates, a Fuze Assembly Mk III, a Heavy Duty Nose Cone Tier 4, 12 Heavy Duty Plates Tier 7, a UHV Sensor, a UHV Emitter and 2 UHV circuits, fits the red matter payload at UHV (2 UHV Field Generators, 2 Quantum Eyes and 2 UHV Emitters), and fills it with 128 Plastic Explosive. Check NEI.%n%nIt digs no crater. A black ball grows from a radius of 2 to 32 blocks at a full casing, eating blocks, killing everything inside (bosses too) and pulling in what is near. It idles for 10 seconds once full-grown and lives 60 seconds at most, a server setting. An Antimatter blast ends it at once. Make one.%n%n[warn]Nothing inside the ball survives. Keep an Antimatter warhead ready if you ever need to stop one.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.ctrVSbsBX6KoGm8-pujtow.name=§5§lEngrave the Schematic
betterquesting.quest.ctrVSbsBX6KoGm8-pujtow.desc=A Galacticraft NASA Workbench builds whatever its schematic tells it to. The Missile Schematic T1 opens the missile's own page, with slots in the shape of the missile.%n%nPut the chip and a red lens in the Laser Engraver at HV (30 seconds); the lens is not used up. Slot the finished schematic into the NASA Workbench and use the Next button to find the missile page. Check NEI for the lens.%n%n[note]Each missile tier has its own chip and schematic. A Tier 2 schematic never opens the Tier 1 page.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.FKODJ5uAW3m6h_n9FGLxtA.name=§8§lMissile Silo
betterquesting.quest.FKODJ5uAW3m6h_n9FGLxtA.desc=The Missile Silo is a GregTech multiblock that loads, fuels and fires missiles for you. A silo shot flies 25 percent farther and scatters half as much as a pad shot.%n%nBuild a 5 by 5 tower around an open 3 by 3 shaft: a Galacticraft launch pad for the shaft floor in a ring of Light or Dark Concrete, three rings of clear glass (Tinkers' Construct or EnderIO), seven rings of concrete (any finish but cobblestone) and a rim of 12 Gantry Beams. The HV controller sits in the middle glass ring. The front is five wide in the glass rings: a 3 by 3 glass window around the controller with a column of concrete or hatches on each side. Fit an Input Bus, an Input Hatch for fuel, an Energy Hatch and a Maintenance Hatch in place of wall, hatch-column, glass or floor-ring blocks. Check the controller's hologram.%n%nThe Energy Hatch sets what it launches: HV for Tier 1, EV for Tier 2, LuV for Tier 3. Feed the bus a body and a warhead and it stands the missile in the shaft. Build a Launch Control into the silo in place of any wall, hatch-column, glass or floor-ring block, one per silo: it fires that silo and no other, runs on the silo's power, and its screen names the silo.
betterquesting.quest.vRWJiomqW3-0yGvcZrRNxw.name=§8§lAbandoned Silo Complex
betterquesting.quest.vRWJiomqW3-0yGvcZrRNxw.desc=Old missile bases lie buried in the Overworld and on every planet with solid ground. A complex is about 240 by 240 blocks and 24 blocks down: a hub, wide halls, 35 to 40 rooms and a gallery of four to ten real silos. On the surface you see only concrete shafts, sometimes a small radar hut, and an escape-ladder trapdoor.%n%nNothing in a complex is better than its planet's ceiling: EV in the Overworld and on the Moon, one voltage tier more for each rocket tier above. Bring back proof: a block of Silo Complex Wall, or a damaged missile body from a salvage chest. The damaged body can't be placed or flown, but it recycles for its plates.%n%n[warn]Every complex has guards at its posts: a couple in an abandoned one, many in an operational one. A post you break stays broken.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.A04ecOa9Va6n70LlUuonMA.name=§8§lRadar Station
betterquesting.quest.A04ecOa9Va6n70LlUuonMA.desc=The radar huts on a complex's surface hold a small radar with its Energy Hatch left out, so they sit dark.%n%nMine the Radar Casing under the radar controller, put an HV Energy Hatch in its place and power it. The radar forms and its dish starts to turn. Link it to an air-defense battery with a data stick, as for any radar. Hold the Radar Casing you mined out and an HV Energy Hatch to finish the quest.
betterquesting.quest.8rPpia-jWum0gSi0ODo2aA.name=§8§lTake Over a Silo
betterquesting.quest.8rPpia-jWum0gSi0ODo2aA.desc=Every silo in a complex is a real Missile Silo with its hatches in place, missing exactly one part: a concrete block where the controller goes, or a concrete block at the foot of the right-hand hatch column where the Energy Hatch goes.%n%nLook for the part in the Safe, Stockpile, Workshop and Control chests, or craft it. Put it in and the silo forms. A found Energy Hatch is EV, which launches up to Tier 2; swap in a LuV hatch for Tier 3. Power it and fire it from its own Launch Control, at the top of the right-hand hatch column, which runs on the silo's power: the complex's silo is yours. Bring back the part you found.%n%n[warn]Clear the guard posts before you start working on the silo.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.Hpt25drUVxG-X28laN9_ng.name=§8§lTitanium Casing
betterquesting.quest.Hpt25drUVxG-X28laN9_ng.desc=The Tier 2 casing is titanium and holds up to 20 charges, four times the Tier 1 casing. The Assembler makes the Inert T2 Warhead at EV from 8 titanium plates, a Fuze Assembly Mk II, a Nose Cone, 12 Heavy Duty Plates Tier 2, an EV Sensor, an EV Emitter and 2 Data circuits. The Mk II fuze is itself an EV Assembler recipe from a Data circuit, a titanium plate and 4 fine electrum wires.%n%nA Tier 2 casing needs a payload before it takes charges: Fragmentation (a titanium Fragmentation Sleeve), Thermobaric (canisters of kerosene), Sonic, Breaching or Contagious, each fitted in the Assembler at EV. Then load 20 Plastic Explosive, in the Assembler or a few at a time in a crafting grid. Check NEI. Make a Tier 2 warhead.%n%n[warn]Tier 2 blasts reach much farther than Tier 1. Read the tooltip's radius before you place one.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.LuSV9ZftUmKkTqpC2lzM8g.name=§8§lTier 2 Missile
betterquesting.quest.LuSV9ZftUmKkTqpC2lzM8g.desc=Tier 2 flies up to 3,000 blocks and carries a titanium-cased warhead (or a lighter one). The build follows the Tier 1 path one step up.%n%nThe Tier 2 chip is made at EV from an Advanced Circuit Board (the epoxy one), 2 Data circuits and 4 fine electrum wires, and engraved with a blue lens. The body page takes four compressed titanium plates, four Heavy Rocket Fins, a Heavy Rocket Engine and a Guidance Computer Mk II or better. It burns 4,000 mB of Dense Hydrazine or a better rocket fuel. Check NEI. Build a Tier 2 body. After that, your EV Assembler builds more of them from the same plates, fins and engine, 2 Data circuits and 250 L of lubricant.%n%n[note]The Heavy Rocket Fins and Engine are Galacticraft parts built from Tier 3 Heavy Duty Plates. This quest opens once you finish the Space Race quests for both.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.jt554mmwW4GO64BnyW_bUw.name=§5§lYour First Warhead
betterquesting.quest.jt554mmwW4GO64BnyW_bUw.desc=Now make it live. Put an Inert T1 Warhead and 1 to 8 Plastic Explosive in a crafting grid and you get a live T1 warhead with that many charges, up to its cap of 5. A bare casing with charges alone is a Condensed warhead, plain high explosive. A casing with a payload becomes that blast type.%n%nPut the warhead back in the grid with more Plastic Explosive to top it up; a load that would pass the cap simply doesn't craft, so nothing is wasted. For automation, the Assembler fills a whole casing at once: an inert warhead and 5 Plastic Explosive on the blast's circuit. Check NEI.%n%nThe tooltip shows the charges, the blast radius and the center damage. Make one warhead, any type, any fill.%n%n[warn]A warhead is a live explosive block. Fire, redstone and nearby explosions all set it off.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.NptPg74nWFqUKvO9--I43g.name=§9§lAnti-Gravity Device
betterquesting.quest.NptPg74nWFqUKvO9--I43g.desc=A back device for flight. It sits in the wings slot and moves you by motion instead of switching on creative flight, so it will not fight with other flight mods.%n%nBuild it in the IV Assembler from two tungstensteel plates, an IV field generator, two IV circuits, the Anti Gravity Core, two Mechanical Parts T3 and a Glider Backpack. It is a tier 5 electric item: charge it in an IV charger or battery buffer.%n%n[note]There is one wings slot, so a jump pack, glider or anti-gravity device are alternatives, not a stack.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.067DdeeDWzCGVka9lF-TwA.name=§9§lAnti Gravity Core
betterquesting.quest.067DdeeDWzCGVka9lF-TwA.desc=The Anti Gravity Core is the part that cancels your weight. It is a nether star surrounded by IV electronics, and the Anti Gravity Device cannot be built without it.%n%nOnly the IV Assembler makes it, from a nether star, an IV emitter, two IV circuits and 1,152 mB of molten Enderium, in 30 seconds. NEI has the recipe if you press R over the core.%n%n[note]A nether star is a Wither drop, so plan the fight before you plan the machine.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.5_c7J85gU2aixhHqkqv1BQ.name=§9§lBlaster Rifle
betterquesting.quest.5_c7J85gU2aixhHqkqv1BQ.desc=The Blaster Rifle is the high-damage energy rifle of the IV tier: a laser with an IV emitter behind it and a Lapotronic Orb for a battery. It is the weapon that makes Laser Rifles feel like toys.%n%nBuild it in the IV Assembler from a Laser Barrel, a Carbon Receiver, a Carbon Gunstock, an IV emitter, a Lapotronic Orb, two IV circuits, tungstensteel plates and screws, and soldering alloy. NEI has the full list.%n%n[note]It is an electric item of tier 5. Only an IV charger or battery buffer will charge it.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.x2lMGKJZWK2Xms6e1LPpgw.name=§9§lDe-Atomizer Pistol
betterquesting.quest.x2lMGKJZWK2Xms6e1LPpgw.desc=A compact energy pistol. The akimbo version holds a pair, one in each hand, for twice the volume of fire.%n%nBuild one in the IV Assembler from a Laser Barrel, a Sonic Emitter, Mechanical Parts T3, a Lapotronic Orb, an IV circuit, titanium and tungstensteel plates and screws. To make the pair, put two De-Atomizer Pistols in the crafting grid. The quest takes either one.%n%n[note]The akimbo pair is an electric item too. Charge it at an IV buffer.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.lH0-MO5VUxWBnzwgiVP8Cw.name=§9§lExo Suit
betterquesting.quest.lH0-MO5VUxWBnzwgiVP8Cw.desc=The Exo Suit is the lighter powered suit. It trades some of the power armor's resistance for a better jump and a lower build cost, and it is the upgrade path for the Advanced Combat armor you built at EV.%n%nEach piece is an upgrade in the IV Assembler: an Advanced Combat piece, Mechanical Parts T3, an IV circuit, an IV electric motor and one or two tungstensteel plates. The Advanced Combat piece is used up and the Exo piece comes out fresh. Charge the chestplate at an IV buffer for the bonuses.%n%n[note]You need both tiers: the Advanced Combat piece is EV work, the upgrade is IV.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.d1LoNVF1UVesinyYYLwYUQ.name=§9§lGolden Revolver
betterquesting.quest.d1LoNVF1UVesinyYYLwYUQ.desc=A showpiece sidearm that is nearly all gold. It is the Revolver's mechanism wrapped in gold, so check its tooltip for the stats.%n%nYou do not build it from scratch. Put a Revolver in the IV Assembler with eight gold plates, two tungstensteel plates and four tungstensteel screws. The Revolver is used up and the new gun comes out fresh, without its camo. Put two golden revolvers in the crafting grid for the akimbo pair.%n%nThe quest takes the single revolver or the pair.
betterquesting.quest.yW5t2nDLXIaIW8EBTAoYYw.name=§9§lPower Armor Era
betterquesting.quest.yW5t2nDLXIaIW8EBTAoYYw.desc=Tungstensteel opens the IV door: blaster rifles, the De-Atomizer pistols, a scatter laser, the golden revolver, and the powered suits that make a player feel like a tank. IV is also where hovering flight arrives, with the Anti Gravity Device.%n%nEverything in this tier is built in the IV Assembler at 7,680 EU/t. Energy guns are tier 5 electric items: they take a Lapotronic Orb as their battery and a good dose of soldering alloy, they come out uncharged, and they only charge in an IV charger or battery buffer. Power armor works the same way.%n%nPlan your power first. A guns-only base can get by on a single IV buffer, but a full suit and a back device want a proper charging line.%n%n[note]Press R over any item in NEI for its exact recipe. Quests only check what you carry; they never take it.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.G3OzWb1tU8i_ycAZ3Q7TMQ.name=§9§lPower Armor
betterquesting.quest.G3OzWb1tU8i_ycAZ3Q7TMQ.desc=The heaviest suit in the mod: very high resistance across damage types, extra health from every piece, and boots with step assist and fall reduction. Its bonuses and its hazard protection only work while the chestplate holds a charge.%n%nEach piece is an IV Assembler recipe of Power Plating, IV circuits, IV electric motors and tungstensteel plates, with a programmed circuit for the piece. The chestplate is the electric part. Charge it at an IV charger or battery buffer. The quest checks the chestplate, but you want all four pieces.%n%n[note]The suit gives heat, cold and electrical protection while charged. Check NEI for the circuit number of each piece.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.nbpw9Ef9VcWXijH89gvslg.name=§9§lPower Plating
betterquesting.quest.nbpw9Ef9VcWXijH89gvslg.desc=Power Plating is the armor core of every powered suit. It is a heavy composite of tungstensteel and epoxy fiber, and it is what the power armor is made of.%n%nCraft two at a time in the IV Assembler from two tungstensteel plates, four Epoxid Fiber Reinforced plates, a Mechanical Parts T3 and two EV circuits. NEI shows the exact recipe. You will use several per suit, so make a stack.%n%n[note]Power armor is far hungrier for Power Plating than the Exo Suit is, so build a lot.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.Bd2n0deSWSu_UTiW5dRIcg.name=§9§lScatter Laser Rifle
betterquesting.quest.Bd2n0deSWSu_UTiW5dRIcg.desc=A laser that fires a spread of five beams. Up close, it is brutal. Further out, the beams spread apart, so keep it for rooms and corridors.%n%nBuild it in the IV Assembler from two Laser Barrels, a Carbon Receiver and Gunstock, two IV emitters, a Lapotronic Orb, two IV circuits, and tungstensteel plates and screws. The extra barrel and emitter pay for the extra beams. NEI has the exact list.%n%n[note]It is a tier 5 electric item, so it charges at an IV buffer only.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.XgnwF9KwUOSKhZqv58tAcQ.name=§9§lPower Armor Era Done
betterquesting.quest.XgnwF9KwUOSKhZqv58tAcQ.desc=Powered suit on your back, blaster in your hands. Every piece of it came out of GregTech machines, not a crafting table.%n%nAt LuV, the Nether Blaster and its Nether Charges move to the Assembly Line. Each needs a research item scanned first, so keep a spare: the Nether Blaster scans a Blaster Rifle, and the charge scans an Advanced Bullet. The gun recipes there also ask for lubricant and more soldering alloy.%n%nHSS-G is the gate material at LuV, so start your HSS-G line now. The coins and the bag below are yours to spend while you set it up.%n%n[note]This capstone pays extra, with three bags. The coins spend at the Vending Machine.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.weAPoFjqUAqgN3uN-vZULg.name=§d§lAlien Blaster
betterquesting.quest.weAPoFjqUAqgN3uN-vZULg.desc=The Alien Blaster is the LuV energy weapon: a bolt that explodes on contact, sets its target on fire, and never breaks a block. It holds twenty-five shots on a full charge.%n%nBuild it in the LuV Assembler from two LuV emitters, a LuV sensor, a Carbon Receiver, a Carbon Gunstock, a Lapotronic Orb II, two LuV circuits, and HSS-G plates and screws, with soldering alloy and lubricant. NEI has the exact recipe. It comes out uncharged.%n%n[note]It is a tier 6 electric item. Charge it in a LuV charger or battery buffer. A lower buffer will not take it.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.GZjqzJtxVuuz-QMPEMSyjg.name=§d§lGolden Gun
betterquesting.quest.GZjqzJtxVuuz-QMPEMSyjg.desc=One shot, one kill. A hit from the Golden Gun kills a living creature outright, and against a boss it takes half of the boss's maximum health. It is a semi-automatic pistol with a one-round chamber, a slow reload and a lot of attitude.%n%nYou make it in the LuV Assembler from a 9mm Pistol, eight gold plates, two LuV circuits and an HSS-G plate. The pistol is used up and the Golden Gun comes out unloaded. Its ammo is the Golden Round from the previous quest.%n%n[note]Creatures that carry damage resistances can still shrug off a hit. Check the tooltip.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.zmUi2Ro9W8GvIl0flLWfkw.name=§d§lGolden Round
betterquesting.quest.zmUi2Ro9W8GvIl0flLWfkw.desc=The Golden Round is the only ammunition the Golden Gun will take: a 9mm bullet dressed in gold. One round is one shot, so you will want a pile of them.%n%nMake them in a LuV Assembler from a 9mm bullet, two gold foils and a gold plate, in 10 seconds. The 9mm bullet itself comes from your LV Ammo Press, so keep that line running. NEI shows the circuit that selects the recipe.
betterquesting.quest._hpgISrBUFq7uIkJaGtsdw.name=§d§lGrim Reaper
betterquesting.quest._hpgISrBUFq7uIkJaGtsdw.desc=Four rocket tubes in one frame. The Grim Reaper holds four rockets and is the heaviest close-range weapon you can build before ZPM.%n%nIt is an upgrade in the LuV Assembler: a Rocket Launcher, three Hardened Steel Barrels for the other tubes, a Carbon Receiver, a LuV electric piston and four HSS-G plates. The launcher is used up. Its ammo is the same Rocket you made at HV.%n%n[warn]The blast radius is the same as the Rocket Launcher's, and four rockets in a row are four chances to hurt yourself.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.ktnOv_R0XRCvYYG60Dpfmg.name=§d§lAssembly-Line Weapons
betterquesting.quest.ktnOv_R0XRCvYYG60Dpfmg.desc=LuV is where GregGuns leaves the plain Assembler behind. The Nether Blaster is built on the Assembly Line, with a research item scanned first, just like GT's own LuV parts. The Alien Blaster, the Grim Reaper and the Golden Gun are LuV Assembler builds, but they all want HSS-G plates and LuV parts.%n%nHSS-G is the gate material, so the first job is a good supply of HSS-G plates and LuV circuits. Energy guns at this tier are tier 6 electric items: they take a Lapotronic Orb II as their battery, come out uncharged, and only charge in a LuV charger or battery buffer.%n%nAssembly Line recipes need a scanned research item and fluids such as soldering alloy, lubricant or lava, and a scanned weapon is matched whatever its charge or wear. Keep a spare of the weapon one tier below the one you want to build.%n%n[note]Press R over any item in NEI for the exact recipe. Quests only check what you carry and never take it.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.SeBngdKKUsysDcTsJvjiqA.name=§d§lNether Blaster
betterquesting.quest.SeBngdKKUsysDcTsJvjiqA.desc=A grenade-style launcher for nether charges. The splash hurts everything near the target, so it is a crowd-clearing weapon and a poor choice at arm's reach.%n%nIt is an Assembly Line build, with the Blaster Rifle as the research item. The inputs are four Cybernetic Parts, a Hardened Steel Barrel, a Pump Mechanism, a Carbon Receiver, a LuV electric piston, two LuV circuits and HSS-G plates and screws, with soldering alloy and lubricant. Cybernetic Parts are the EV bio chain's product. NEI shows the rest.%n%n[warn]The splash can reach you. Keep your distance.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.ID9t77f7UgaJ8R1kiS9a8A.name=§d§lNether Charge
betterquesting.quest.ID9t77f7UgaJ8R1kiS9a8A.desc=The Nether Charge is a small, nasty explosive packed with netherrack and soul sand. The Nether Blaster fires it, and it blows a small area apart.%n%nIt is an Assembly Line recipe: netherrack dust, soul sand, HSS-G plates, a LuV circuit, gunpowder and 4,000 mB of lava make sixteen charges in 20 seconds. The research item is an Advanced Bullet, so scan one in a Research Station first. NEI lists the full recipe.%n%n[warn]Charges are explosives. Store them away from your furnaces and your temper.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.LxA9nvbuWduXmAVgymB0Sg.name=§d§lLuV Arms Done
betterquesting.quest.LxA9nvbuWduXmAVgymB0Sg.desc=Alien Blaster in one hand and a four-barrel Grim Reaper in the other. That is the Assembly Line paying off, and it is a long way from the bronze steam armor you started in.%n%nZPM is the top of the tree. Naquadah alloy is the gate, the Nuclear Death Ray is its crown, and the Nuke Launcher is its loudest voice. Both are Assembly Line builds with research items you have already made: the Death Ray scans an Alien Blaster, and the Nuke Launcher scans a Grim Reaper.%n%nSo keep a spare of each. A scanned weapon is matched whatever its charge or wear, so a used one works.%n%n[note]This capstone pays double, with an extra bag. Spend the coins at the Vending Machine.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.Mz-uO4DjXsKUCga3SdfpiQ.name=§2§l9mm Rounds
betterquesting.quest.Mz-uO4DjXsKUCga3SdfpiQ.desc=The 9mm bullet feeds the pistol and the revolver, and it is the cheapest round you will make. A single run in the Ammo Press takes sixteen brass foils, sixteen lead rounds and two gunpowder and produces sixteen bullets.%n%nBrass foil comes from the Bending Machine, and lead rounds from the Lathe or from a nugget and a file. Check the Ammo Press tab in NEI for the exact recipe. Rounds take a while by design, so queue several runs.%n%n[note]One batch makes sixteen bullets, enough to fill five pistol magazines.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.uDmM8VcaUEejFs-ZPe9QRQ.name=§2§lAmmo Press
betterquesting.quest.uDmM8VcaUEejFs-ZPe9QRQ.desc=Ammo is made in the GregGuns Ammo Press, not in a GregTech Assembler. It has its own recipe map: bullets, shells, empty magazines and loaded magazines, each pressed from GregTech parts and gunpowder. Build the LV press and everything in this chapter becomes possible.%n%nIts hand recipe is like GregTech's own basic machines: an LV hull, a motor, a piston, conveyors, circuits and cable. Check NEI for the exact grid. The Steam press you may already own runs the same recipes more slowly.%n%n[note]A machine can run any recipe at or below its tier. The LV press covers every LV round and magazine; MV and HV presses are needed for later calibers.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.OIA2p5kmWNCbwJq3dLyAHQ.name=§2§lBandages
betterquesting.quest.OIA2p5kmWNCbwJq3dLyAHQ.desc=A bandage is the cheapest healing you can carry. Using one takes about three seconds, heals one heart and gives Regeneration I for a while. Two come out of a single LV Assembler run of three string, a slimeball and a steel ring.%n%nHold four to finish this quest. Keep a few in your hotbar before you go near any soldier.%n%n[note]The Medkit in the Gear chapter heals more, but it needs aluminum.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.XzCp7O1kWYW7UEyUcRinjQ.name=§2§lBolt Action Rifle
betterquesting.quest.XzCp7O1kWYW7UEyUcRinjQ.desc=Long range and slow to cycle. The Bolt Action Rifle hits much harder than any LV sidearm and has a real scope: right-click to zoom in, which also tightens your spread, and line up the shot. It holds six rounds.%n%nThe recipe uses the Hardened Steel Barrel and Iron Receiver from the parts quest, a Wooden Stock, a glass lens for the scope, and steel plates, screws and a spring. Rifle Bullets come from the Ammo Press: brass foil, steel rounds and gunpowder.%n%n[note]Zoom shrinks your field of view and narrows the spread while it is active.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.apiZbYKfWCSb47TsYpHd0Q.name=§2§lT1 Combat Armor
betterquesting.quest.apiZbYKfWCSb47TsYpHd0Q.desc=Steel plate and Tanned Leather, pressed in the LV Assembler. The Soldier's set is the first armor that protects better than the hand-made sets: three steel plates in every piece but the boots, which take two, plus cloth, and a full set beats the Steam armor. The Soldier's Vest is the quest item.%n%nStock up on Tanned Leather, because the vest alone eats five. Your LV Chemical Bath makes it from two leather in phosphoric acid, with no drying rack to wait on. Helmet, vest, pants and boots each use their own circuit number in the Assembler, and NEI shows each one.%n%n[note]Armor value shows on the tooltip. Compare sets before you commit plates.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.hYUeOT7cXjOoCT5LMikuZA.name=§2§lSteel-Age Firearms
betterquesting.quest.hYUeOT7cXjOoCT5LMikuZA.desc=Steel changes everything. At LV your guns move from the crafting table to the GregTech Assembler, your ammunition moves to the GregGuns Ammo Press, and a handful of new weapons become possible: a pistol, a revolver, a sawed-off shotgun and a bolt-action rifle, plus steel armor and the first melee tools.%n%nThe gate is steel. Nearly every LV recipe in this chapter uses it, and the last step is always an LV machine. Hold eight steel plates to open the chapter; you will use them up quickly.%n%nStart with the Ammo Press, because every gun in this chapter is useless without it. Then make 9mm bullets, build the parts for your first pistol, and branch out to the rifle and shotgun when you have lead and brass to spare. The grenade, bandages and armor quests are optional, but the loot bags are worth the trip.%n%n[note]Press R on any gun in NEI to see its recipe. Every LV gun is built in an LV Assembler.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.boi3n217UI6XIPY0yyxEVQ.name=§2§lMagazines
betterquesting.quest.boi3n217UI6XIPY0yyxEVQ.desc=A magazine is built in two steps in the same Ammo Press. First press empty magazines: two steel plates, eight small steel springs and Mechanical Parts T2 make eight. Then fill them: four empties and twelve 9mm bullets make four loaded magazines.%n%nYou can also fill one by hand: put an empty magazine and three 9mm bullets together in a crafting grid. The press is just faster, and the pipes in the Ammo Logistics chapter can run it for you.%n%n[note]A loaded pistol magazine holds eighteen rounds. Sneak and right-click it to take the bullets back out.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.chM3O2OvW4ilHfb1FAhltA.name=§2§lKnife or Crowbar
betterquesting.quest.chM3O2OvW4ilHfb1FAhltA.desc=Melee tools never run dry. The Combat Knife is a steel blade for when the magazine is empty; the Crowbar is a tool as much as a weapon, and it mines blocks like an iron pickaxe. Either one completes this quest, and both are cheap.%n%nBoth are LV Assembler recipes. The knife takes two steel plates, a rubber plate and two screws; the crowbar takes long steel rods, a plate and a screw. Check NEI for the exact amounts.%n%n[note]A crowbar in your hotbar means one less pickaxe to carry on a bunker raid.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.QjKNH4ynWAi5zcbD1AJNMA.name=§2§lGun Parts at LV
betterquesting.quest.QjKNH4ynWAi5zcbD1AJNMA.desc=Steel guns are built from steel parts, and three of them turn up in almost every LV recipe. The Hardened Steel Barrel (a steel pipe, two rings and a plate) is the bore of the pistol and the rifle. The Iron Receiver (three iron plates, Mechanical Parts and two steel screws) is the action of the bolt-action rifle. Mechanical Parts T2 (small steel gears, springs and screws) is the clockwork inside nearly everything.%n%nAll three are LV Assembler recipes, and NEI shows the inputs. Hold one of each to finish this quest.%n%n[note]Mechanical Parts T2 are also an input to empty magazines, so make extra.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.mJR67SnRUAyj7d-tQP9low.name=§2§l9mm Pistol
betterquesting.quest.mJR67SnRUAyj7d-tQP9low.desc=Your first real sidearm. The 9mm Pistol is semi-automatic and fed from an eighteen-round magazine, so a reload is one key press instead of the Hand Cannon's slow single shot.%n%nIt is an LV Assembler recipe. The inputs are a Hardened Steel Barrel, Mechanical Parts T2, steel plates, rubber plates, steel screws and a spring: the parts from the last quest plus a little rubber, standing in for a plastic grip. NEI has the exact list.%n%nThe pistol takes 9mm Pistol Magazines, filled from three bullets each; see the Magazines quest next.%n%n[note]Press Reload with a loaded magazine in your inventory. Sneak and right-click a magazine to empty it back into loose rounds.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.NsiOegLwXQeQiJScpSPrjA.name=§2§lRevolver
betterquesting.quest.NsiOegLwXQeQiJScpSPrjA.desc=A heavier sidearm with six chambers and a bit more punch per shot than the pistol, at the cost of a longer reload. The Revolver uses loose 9mm bullets instead of a magazine: one bullet reloads all six chambers.%n%nIt is built in the LV Assembler from an Iron Barrel, Mechanical Parts, a Wooden Stock, steel plates and screws, and a spring. Compare its damage and range with the pistol on the tooltips and keep the one you like; two Revolvers combine into Akimbo Revolvers at a crafting table.%n%n[note]The Revolver is the cheapest gun to keep fed, because one loose bullet fills it.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.PUU_uhcLWImmqnZiZfJu-g.name=§2§lSawed Off
betterquesting.quest.PUU_uhcLWImmqnZiZfJu-g.desc=Two barrels, two shells, and an apology to whatever is in front of you. The Sawed Off fires a spray of pellets: ruinous at point-blank range and nearly useless at a distance. It holds two shells, and a reload tops up only what you have fired.%n%nBuild it in an LV Assembler from two Iron Barrels, a Wooden Stock, a steel plate, screws and a spring. Its ammo is the Shotgun Shell, which the Ammo Press makes from eight brass foils, twenty-four lead rounds and four gunpowder per batch of eight; the Ammo Logistics chapter walks through it.%n%n[warn]Do not stand in the open with it. Anything that survives the first two shells is already next to you.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.yVLRYxizXrSazsohXoKK1w.name=§2§lStielgranate
betterquesting.quest.yVLRYxizXrSazsohXoKK1w.desc=A classic stick grenade: a steel head packed with gunpowder on a wooden handle. It deals heavy blast damage in a radius of about five blocks and bounces a few times before it settles, so you can throw it around a corner. Sixteen come out of one LV Assembler run.%n%nThe recipe is two steel plates, four gunpowder and a wooden stick. Hold sixteen to finish the quest. Hold right click to wind up a throw; the longer you hold, the farther it goes.%n%n[warn]The fuse is ten seconds long and the blast hurts you too. Throw it and step back. By default it does not break blocks, but a server can turn that on.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.q59wXd1mV1WcX1YeUf6dfA.name=§2§lSteel Age Done
betterquesting.quest.q59wXd1mV1WcX1YeUf6dfA.desc=You have a press, a pistol, a revolver, a shotgun, a rifle and steel armor. LV is done. The next gate is aluminum, and with it come automatic weapons, grenades with real fragments, and the first serious armor.%n%nAluminum is a GregTech project in its own right: bauxite, electrolysis, and an MV power setup. Take your time. Everything you built here keeps working at MV, and a higher-tier machine runs lower-tier recipes faster.%n%nHold four aluminum plates to close the chapter and take the big loot bag. Spend some of the winnings on ammo, because MV guns burn through it.%n%n[note]The MV chapter opens from the pack's MV quests, not from this one. You can start it any time.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.QuPctiU0UTysPZKi-tEFjA.name=§5§lArmory Gantry
betterquesting.quest.QuPctiU0UTysPZKi-tEFjA.desc=When one bench is too slow, build the Armory Gantry: a hall of two to eight bays, each a portal frame with a hoist on its beam and a repair cradle on its floor, so each cycle mends up to one item per bay. Armor goes in an Input Bus, parts alongside, and repaired items come out of an Output Bus.%n%nThe controller is HV, and the weakest Energy Hatch sets the highest tier of item it repairs. It needs Input and Output Buses, an Energy Hatch and a Maintenance Hatch, Gantry Casings, glass of any tier and the interior parts: gearbox, motors, frame box hooks, floor rails, pipe runs and a lamp in every bay.%n%n[note]Use the controller's structure hints to see what is missing.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.wiZf_nJjUDWSzPXMNLmtlw.name=§2§lGregGuns Machines
betterquesting.quest.wiZf_nJjUDWSzPXMNLmtlw.desc=Almost everything you build in GregGuns runs on plain GregTech machines: assemblers, presses, benches. Only a handful of machines are GregGuns' own, and they are GregTech machines too, so most take EU and follow GT's voltage rules.%n%nThe Repair Bench and the Armory Gantry mend gear. The Turret and the Rampart defend your base. The Camo Bench cycles the camouflage of guns and armor, and it needs no power. The Ammo Press and the Ammunition Works make ammunition, which the ammo chapter covers.%n%nStart with the cheapest and most fun one: build a Camo Bench. It is an LV machine, so you can build it right now. Check NEI for the recipe.%n%n[note]Single blocks come in tiers. A bench or turret must be at least as high a tier as the item it works on.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.HJVu3hFmXUeXp1q2JY1lcA.name=§6§lMending Armor
betterquesting.quest.HJVu3hFmXUeXp1q2JY1lcA.desc=Repairs cost parts: a plate of the set's gate material and Tanned Leather. T1 Combat armor is gated by steel, so a worn Soldier's Vest takes steel plates and cloth, and the more damaged it is, the more parts it takes, up to two plates and two Tanned Leather. Bandit (Scout) gear mends with Tanned Leather alone.%n%nGather a T1 Combat chestplate, two Tanned Leather and two steel plates, then use the bench's Chest button. The bench accepts any mod's plate of the right material.%n%n[note]GregTech tools keep their wear in their own data and the bench never touches them.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.z8faDvh0UvemqxE8s6CRxQ.name=§6§lRepair Bench
betterquesting.quest.z8faDvh0UvemqxE8s6CRxQ.desc=Armor wears down in a fight, and the Repair Bench puts it right. Put worn armor and the repair parts in its nine slots, press Head, Chest, Legs, Feet or Held, and the bench restores the piece to full if it holds enough parts. A repair is all or nothing: if you are short, nothing is consumed.%n%nThe bench is a GregTech machine and draws EU for each job. A repair takes two seconds plus up to eight more depending on the damage, at half the recipe voltage of the bench's tier. Build the LV bench for LV gear and the MV bench for MV gear. A bench can only mend items of its own tier or lower.%n%nCheck NEI for the recipe.
betterquesting.quest.F4G1fstlX7WJJh6m9opOfA.name=§5§lTurret
betterquesting.quest.F4G1fstlX7WJJh6m9opOfA.desc=A Turret holds one gun from your own loadout on a platform, shoots with the real ammo you feed it, and comes with a 30-health mounted turret that heals when powered and respawns after it dies. It guards your base with the same guns you carry.%n%nIt runs on EU at its tier voltage. Its tier must be at least that of its gun, so an MV turret fires MV guns and an HV turret HV guns. You load the gun, magazines or rounds, and an armor plate in its slots. Build an MV or HV turret.%n%n[note]The Rampart is the multiblock version: up to ten mounts on one ammo and power feed. Check NEI.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.XCqKCGtOU02fIt4JMyjTzw.name=§5§lPowering the Turret
betterquesting.quest.XCqKCGtOU02fIt4JMyjTzw.desc=The turret takes EU at its tier. Feed it from a battery buffer or generator through a cable of the right voltage. GregTech's usual overvoltage rules apply, so a cable carrying too much power for it will damage it.%n%nIts screen shows its state (On guard, No gun, No power) and its stored EU. Build a plate of armor for it: steel plates are LV, aluminum MV.%n%n[note]A powered turret heals its mount, so keep a buffer in reserve.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.qz639_9iXPChHoN46iJdPQ.name=§5§lFriend or Foe
betterquesting.quest.qz639_9iXPChHoN46iJdPQ.desc=A turret shoots every hostile mob. What it does to players depends on its Security button: set above public it shoots any player who is not you or your friend, where a friend is an ally or better on your ServerUtilities team. Without ServerUtilities only the owner is a friend. Target Animals makes it shoot passive creatures too.%n%nPut a gun and magazines in the turret and set its security. A Thompson with two magazines will do.%n%n[warn]A turret fires on players it does not know, including a visiting friend who has not joined your team.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.yOzpMokqUwe66PdRL7Lcyg.name=§6§lAkimbo
betterquesting.quest.yOzpMokqUwe66PdRL7Lcyg.desc=Two guns, one trigger. Akimbo Pistols and Akimbo Revolvers are made by combining two identical sidearms in a crafting grid. No machine is needed, and no offhand slot either: the akimbo gun is a single item that fires with alternating hands. Either one completes this quest.%n%nThe pair doubles your clip, and a reload uses two magazines (or two bullets for the revolvers). Put the gun in a crafting grid alone and it splits back into the two originals, ammo included.%n%n[note]Two Mac10s make Akimbo Mac10s the same way, and those fire both guns on every pull.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.lypD0jUiVxK_GAPc5kkxMw.name=§6§lCombat Shotgun
betterquesting.quest.lypD0jUiVxK_GAPc5kkxMw.desc=The big brother of the Sawed Off. Eight shells in the tube, and one reload tops up every empty spot with the same Shotgun Shells, so your LV shell production keeps it fed. Pellets spread wide, so it is devastating up close and weak at range.%n%nIt is built in an MV Assembler from a Hardened Steel Barrel, a Steel Receiver, a Plastic Gun Stock, steel rods for the pump tube, and aluminum plates, screws and springs.%n%n[note]Reload between fights, not during them. A reload takes two and a half seconds.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.CxLbdj1wXiCSjt4IO5DHvA.name=§6§lFlashbang
betterquesting.quest.CxLbdj1wXiCSjt4IO5DHvA.desc=Blinds and stuns instead of killing. Players caught in the flash go blind, then reel; mobs are slowed and weakened and forget who they were hunting. It does no damage and breaks no blocks, which makes it perfect for clearing a camp.%n%nSixteen come out of one MV Assembler run of two aluminum plates, four magnesium dust and two gunpowder. The fuse is only two seconds, and a wall between you and the blast blocks the flash entirely.%n%n[note]Turn your back before it pops. The flash is strongest when you are looking at it. It affects the thrower too.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.SkjH3vntWvqub9jvearFeg.name=§6§lFrag Grenade
betterquesting.quest.SkjH3vntWvqub9jvearFeg.desc=The Frag Grenade is a hand grenade that means it. It blasts a radius of six blocks, and afterward sixty-four steel fragments fly out and hit whatever is in line. It is deadly in the open and up close, and a wall or another body shields you.%n%nSixteen come out of one MV Assembler run: two aluminum plates, sixteen steel rounds and two TNT blocks. Hold sixteen to finish the quest.%n%n[warn]The fuse is six seconds, the thrower takes the blast like everyone else, and fragments need clear air. Throw from behind cover. Block damage is off unless the server turns it on.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.liaFkCI8Wret4DrZAA9GQw.name=§6§lAluminum-Age Arms
betterquesting.quest.liaFkCI8Wret4DrZAA9GQw.desc=MV is where firepower goes automatic. Aluminum unlocks the SMGs, the assault rifles and a combat shotgun, plus grenades, the flashbang, three more armor sets and the akimbo pairs you can make from your LV sidearms. The guns, grenades and armor are MV Assembler recipes with aluminum in them; the akimbo pairs are crafted by hand.%n%nAmmunition changes too. SMGs and assault rifles take their own magazines, which are pressed in an MV Ammo Press, so build one (an MV press also runs every LV recipe, faster). The magazines need aluminum plates and springs.%n%nHold eight aluminum plates to open the chapter. The thick line runs through the parts, the SMG and the rifles; grenades, armor and the akimbo guns hang off to the side.%n%n[note]You can run LV recipes in an MV machine, so one MV press and one MV assembler cover everything so far.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.BOcA_OeIUSiErFpkmViT6w.name=§6§lMac10
betterquesting.quest.BOcA_OeIUSiErFpkmViT6w.desc=A compact automatic SMG with a thirty-two round clip. The Mac10 trades the Thompson's wooden furniture for steel parts: a Hardened Steel Barrel, a Steel Receiver and a polyethylene plate, plus aluminum plates, screws and springs, assembled in an MV Assembler.%n%nIt uses the same SMG magazines as the Thompson. Two Mac10s combine into Akimbo Mac10s in a crafting grid, and the pair fires both guns on every pull.%n%n[note]The Steel Receiver is an MV part with its own quest. See MV Gun Parts.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.NxGsIdieWcack69uLkOSiQ.name=§6§lMV Gun Parts
betterquesting.quest.NxGsIdieWcack69uLkOSiQ.desc=MV rifles and shotguns are built around two new parts. The Steel Receiver (three steel plates, Mechanical Parts T2 and two aluminum screws) is a tougher action than the iron one. The Plastic Gun Stock (three polyethylene plates and two aluminum screws) replaces wood.%n%nBoth are MV Assembler recipes, and NEI shows the inputs. Hold one of each to finish this quest. Polyethylene is GregTech's plastic; you will meet it in the oil chapters of the pack.%n%n[note]The M4, the Combat Shotgun and the Mac10 all use the Steel Receiver.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.gPKVACp0U7-bbCtwGWRsHQ.name=§6§lM4 or AK47
betterquesting.quest.gPKVACp0U7-bbCtwGWRsHQ.desc=Assault rifles are the backbone of MV. Both the M4 and the AK47 fire automatically from a thirty-round Assault Rifle Magazine, which is not the same as an SMG magazine: each loaded one takes three Rifle Bullets, the same rounds as the bolt rifle. Either rifle completes this quest.%n%nThe M4 has a scope (right-click to zoom) and uses the Steel Receiver and Plastic Gun Stock. The AK47 is cheaper, with an Iron Receiver and a Wooden Stock plus a couple of wooden sticks. Both use a Hardened Steel Barrel. Pick the one you can afford.%n%n[note]Assault Rifle Magazines have their own empty recipe in the MV press: three aluminum plates, eight springs and Mechanical Parts T2 make eight.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.P59k8AiKWgmAaH75tkGLXg.name=§6§lSMG Magazines
betterquesting.quest.P59k8AiKWgmAaH75tkGLXg.desc=The SMG magazine has its own two-step recipe. In an MV Ammo Press, two aluminum plates, nine small aluminum springs and Mechanical Parts T2 make eight empty magazines. Then four empties and eight 9mm bullets make four loaded ones.%n%nNote what it eats: the SMG shares the 9mm bullet with the pistol and revolver, so the LV production line you built already feeds it. Each loaded magazine takes two bullets.%n%n[note]Only an MV or higher press runs MV recipes. The LV press will not start them.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.F6wvUKf0XpmlAqliuUYTtw.name=§6§lAluminum Age Done
betterquesting.quest.F6wvUKf0XpmlAqliuUYTtw.desc=You have an SMG, an assault rifle and aluminum armor, and the supply line to feed them. The combat shotgun and grenades round out the kit if you have not built them yet. MV is done. Stainless steel is the next gate, and with it come heavy weapons, high-caliber rifles and rockets.%n%nStainless steel needs a proper alloy line: iron, nickel, manganese and chromium, smelted in the Electric Blast Furnace. It is a long project, so get comfortable. Everything you built at MV keeps working, and an HV Ammo Press will run MV recipes faster.%n%nHold four stainless steel plates to close the chapter and collect the big loot bag. Stock up on ammo before you go.%n%n[note]The HV chapter opens from the pack's HV quests. You can start it any time.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.eWJcwTF7Uqq5lbmE95P4Fg.name=§6§lT2 Armor
betterquesting.quest.eWJcwTF7Uqq5lbmE95P4Fg.desc=Aluminum armor comes in three flavors. Combat is aluminum plates and Tanned Leather, the all-rounder. Commando is aluminum, rubber and a glass pane, lighter and built to move. The Ranger Veteran set upgrades a Combat piece with lead plates and more Tanned Leather for the most protection. Any one chestplate completes this quest.%n%nAll three are MV Assembler recipes; NEI shows every piece. Tanned Leather and rubber are the common inputs.%n%n[note]Armor value shows on the tooltip. Compare sets before you commit plates.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.ylGIBgZrXvKLESd_27N5MA.name=§6§lThompson SMG
betterquesting.quest.ylGIBgZrXvKLESd_27N5MA.desc=Fast, light automatic fire for crowds of anything. The Thompson keeps firing while you hold the trigger and gets through an SMG magazine quickly, so it shines at short range and runs dry if you waste it.%n%nIt is built in an MV Assembler from an Iron Barrel, an Iron Receiver, a Wooden Stock, aluminum plates, screws and springs. It shoots the same 9mm bullets as your pistol, loaded into SMG magazines. If you want a bigger clip, look at the Mac10 next door.%n%n[note]Fire in short bursts and keep a spare magazine loaded.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.lYUjVBo5WV29u03j0mJOMw.name=§8§lAlien Bug
betterquesting.quest.lYUjVBo5WV29u03j0mJOMw.desc=A fast, wall-climbing spider-like creature from the Alien Bug Nest. Find a nest in a sandy biome: the bug spawns from the vanilla mob spawner inside.%n%nIt drops string and spider eyes. Check the nest quest in the site chapter for what else the nest holds.
betterquesting.quest.syP7nK4rUwirzv6x-PBQcA.name=§6§lArmy Soldiers
betterquesting.quest.syP7nK4rUwirzv6x-PBQcA.desc=Army Soldiers are disciplined, armored in T2 Combat gear and armed with M4 rifles, Combat Shotguns or bolt-action rifles. They do not wander the countryside. They come out of Military Camps, the Aircraft Carrier and silo guard posts, so you have to go to them.%n%nKill five. They drop rifle bullets, shells, iron and Tanned Leather.
betterquesting.quest.kYI6SLykVpiRBdyquFfUMA.name=§2§lBandits
betterquesting.quest.kYI6SLykVpiRBdyquFfUMA.desc=Bandits are the first enemies that carry real LV firepower: 9mm pistols, revolvers, sawed-offs, bolt-action rifles and now and then an AK-47 or Thompson. They wear Scout gear.%n%nThey drop 9mm rounds, shells and rifle bullets, so they are a free ammo supply. Kill four.%n%n[note]Outcasts, their heavily armed cousins, appear only from spawn eggs.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.4gg1AG4HXMadTcKsWXWc8w.name=§6§lCommandos
betterquesting.quest.4gg1AG4HXMadTcKsWXWc8w.desc=Commandos are Army elite in T2 Commando armor with M4 rifles. They drop explosive charges, steel ingots and rubber plates. Find them at Aircraft Carriers and silo guard posts.%n%nArmor up and kill three.
betterquesting.quest.KX-pQPLZWgSCTyjXwnLAJg.name=§8§lCyberdemon
betterquesting.quest.KX-pQPLZWgSCTyjXwnLAJg.desc=A fire-immune Nether brute armed with the Nether Blaster, the Cyberdemon is a Nether mob that also comes from a spawn egg or an admin command. It drops ghast tears, blaze rods and cybernetic parts.%n%n[warn]It hits hard. Bring good armor.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.R02XjcLfWyuLzIo6xjcahQ.name=§9§lDictator Dave
betterquesting.quest.R02XjcLfWyuLzIo6xjcahQ.desc=A secret mini-boss with 100 health, Dave fires a Golden Revolver and wears a beret. He does not spawn on his own: he comes from a spawn egg, an admin command or a custom spawner.%n%nHe drops the Golden Revolver and some 9mm rounds.
betterquesting.quest.P0cM5jjnWWi0jPfg1nfTaw.name=§5§lAttack Helicopter
betterquesting.quest.P0cM5jjnWWi0jPfg1nfTaw.desc=A flying boss with 100 health and its own boss bar, the Attack Helicopter circles you with machine-gun bursts and rockets. Bring launchers and cover. It drops rifle bullets, rockets, cybernetic parts and iron blocks.%n%n[note]Breaking a Camp Flag calls one in. An admin can turn the helicopter setting off under npcs in the GregGuns config.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.a315yLzbWASFSYtqJlkyDQ.name=§c§lHostile Factions
betterquesting.quest.a315yLzbWASFSYtqJlkyDQ.desc=Soldiers, bandits and the walking dead share the Overworld with you, and most of them are armed. Some carry real guns, some drop real ammo, and a few drop things you cannot easily make yet. Hunting them is the cheapest way to stock up on rounds and cloth, and every hunt in this chapter pays out.%n%nZombies, skeletons, bandits and Psycho Steve spawn on their own in the Overworld. The rest come from structures: camp flags send out soldiers, and a Big Bunker or a silo complex holds ordinary vanilla mob spawners with an NPC spinning inside. A spawner only works while you are within 24 blocks, caps how many of its mob stand around it, and drops nothing when broken. GregTech makes spawners very slow to mine by hand, so treat them as a farm, not a trophy.%n%nSome spawns are Infernal: a glowing name, a boss bar and a pile of modifiers. Elite mobs have up to five, ultra up to ten, infernal more, and each rank drops better GregGuns gear (LV, MV, and MV with a rare HV roll). Structure guards from spawners roll for Infernal too, at the same odds.%n%n[note]Go armed: hold a Hand Cannon and 16 stone bullets to start the chapter.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.YGbgOq4_WZWQaK62pgw0zw.name=§c§lSkeleton Soldiers
betterquesting.quest.YGbgOq4_WZWQaK62pgw0zw.desc=Armed skeletons shoot back with revolvers, Thompsons and the occasional Hand Cannon, and some wear Soldier's or Bandit helmets and boots. They are more accurate than zombies, so use cover and keep moving.%n%nFive kills earns the reward. They drop bones, coal and gunpowder.
betterquesting.quest.80v0VhPfVBKUVzQY1NhNKQ.name=§2§lPsycho Steve
betterquesting.quest.80v0VhPfVBKUVzQY1NhNKQ.desc=A chainsaw-wielding mini-boss in miner gear, Steve is rare (a spawn weight of 1) and has 75 health, so he soaks up bullets while he runs you down. Keep your distance.%n%nHe always drops his Chainsaw and a handful of fuel tanks.%n%n[warn]He is a melee threat. Do not fight him in a corridor.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.HNX5vy9IXyWXlDl05MGb6w.name=§c§lWalking Dead
betterquesting.quest.HNX5vy9IXyWXlDl05MGb6w.desc=Three kinds of zombie carry guns instead of just groaning. Farmers and miners are the common ones and carry hoes, picks and the odd Hand Cannon. Soldiers are rarer, tougher and often wear Soldier's armor.%n%nKill three of each. They drop Tanned Leather and gunpowder, plus food, coal, iron or ammo depending on the kind, which feeds your armor and ammo crafting.
betterquesting.quest.Tkq4h6W7X9WBrKfavb-TUQ.name=§6§lBig Bunker
betterquesting.quest.Tkq4h6W7X9WBrKfavb-TUQ.desc=The Big Bunker is a concrete fortress with Weapon and Reinforced chests throughout and a spawner room, and its loot reaches MV: Thompsons, MAC-10s, AK-47s, M4s and their magazines. Zombie Soldiers, Farmers and Miners spill out of the vanilla mob spawners inside, three at a time, up to five of each at once.%n%nKill three Zombie Soldiers and take an MV gun out of the chests. Breaking a spawner by hand takes a long time, so farm it instead.%n%n[warn]The zombies carry guns and the bunker is dark. Bring light and armor.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.OKZ9OGCiXDOv_DYYvjYKlA.name=§6§lMilitary Camp
betterquesting.quest.OKZ9OGCiXDOv_DYYvjYKlA.desc=A Military Camp is a ring of tents, barracks, bunkers and a flag post, and soldiers pour out of the flag as long as you stay near. Barracks hold T1 and T2 Combat armor, and the crates hold MV weapons.%n%nKill four Army Soldiers and bring back a piece of T2 Combat armor from the barracks. You can also craft it, but the barracks are free.%n%n[note]The flag drops a single iron ingot when broken; the guns are in the crates.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.l1PRgHu1Vley1Cdb74iqiA.name=§2§lDungeon Weapons
betterquesting.quest.l1PRgHu1Vley1Cdb74iqiA.desc=Roguelike dungeons sink deep into the ground, floor after floor of spawners, traps and chests. Go down armed: a gun for the corridors and a blade for when the ammo runs dry.%n%nCarry one gun and one blade: a pistol, revolver or sawed-off, and a Combat Knife or Crowbar. GregGuns ruins and camps keep them in their chests, every one of them is an LV Assembler recipe, and some servers stock dungeon chests with them too.%n%n[warn]Dungeons are full of vanilla mobs and traps. Bring armor, light and an exit plan.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.hT8IW5j8U86nS3mZn_bUiw.name=§c§lRuins and Camps
betterquesting.quest.hT8IW5j8U86nS3mZn_bUiw.desc=Factories, houses, bunkers, camps and ships dot the Overworld, and their chests hold GregGuns gear you would otherwise have to craft. Each structure draws from loot tables with a tier ceiling. In the Overworld the small ruins stop at LV and everything bigger stops at MV, so a trip is worth it at any stage but never hands you the next tier early.%n%nStructures also spawn on Ross128b and its moon, where each one rolls its own ceiling and can hold far better loot. An admin can turn any of them off in the worldgen section of the GregGuns config. Vanilla chests fill when the world generates; Weapon and Reinforced chests fill the first time someone opens them.%n%nEach quest in this chapter asks you to bring back something you can find there. Craftable items count too, so you can also build your way through, but the loot is free.%n%n[note]Go armed: carry a Hand Cannon and some stone bullets before you leave the base.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.zwiUSYU8WnWJNAd05U6gCg.name=§8§lAlien Bug Nest
betterquesting.quest.zwiUSYU8WnWJNAd05U6gCg.desc=The Alien Bug Nest is a hive of hard resin walls and soft egg clusters, with a climbable slime trail down its entrance shaft and a vanilla mob spawner for the Alien Bug at its heart. Nothing else generates resin or eggs, so mining some is proof you were there.%n%nBring back four resin and two egg clusters. Resin is hard to mine; eggs are soft.%n%n[note]An admin can stop nests from generating with the Alien Bug Nest setting in the worldgen section of the GregGuns config.[/note]
betterquesting.quest._UPNUiNWV1O-jO_H9CIL7Q.name=§6§lCarrier and Submarine
betterquesting.quest._UPNUiNWV1O-jO_H9CIL7Q.desc=The Aircraft Carrier and the Submarine are the largest structures, and their chests hold MV weapons and grenades. The carrier also carries a flag that sends out Army Soldiers and Commandos, up to nine at a time, so bring backup.%n%nBring back an MV gun and four Stielgranates from the chests. Both are craftable, but the ships hold plenty.%n%n[warn]Commandos carry explosive charges. Do not stand in a corridor.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.sv2TkVqVX8a9uLShdPxeiw.name=§2§lSmall Ruins
betterquesting.quest.sv2TkVqVX8a9uLShdPxeiw.desc=The small factory, train station, gas station and medium house are the easy stops. Their chests draw from the LV weapon table: 9mm and shotgun rounds, revolvers, sawed-offs and the occasional Hand Cannon. The medium house also holds Reinforced Chests of GregTech ingots (tin, copper, lead, iron) and a few Weapon Chests.%n%nBring back a revolver, sawed-off or Hand Cannon, and some 9mm or shotgun rounds. The revolver and sawed-off are LV builds and the Hand Cannon is steam age, so check NEI if the chests are not generous.
betterquesting.quest.B5FdBkr1X5auKNEWfCQlrw.name=Trigger: EV Tier Skip
betterquesting.quest.B5FdBkr1X5auKNEWfCQlrw.desc=No Description
betterquesting.quest._5Sldx3_Ub2sSg-JopCQFA.name=Trigger: HV Tier Skip
betterquesting.quest._5Sldx3_Ub2sSg-JopCQFA.desc=No Description
betterquesting.quest.k7wUDquJVQmraumbOZepmA.name=Trigger: IV Tier Skip
betterquesting.quest.k7wUDquJVQmraumbOZepmA.desc=No Description
betterquesting.quest.AWPf1dBEWb-1f6Fu0hDXKA.name=Trigger: LuV Tier Skip
betterquesting.quest.AWPf1dBEWb-1f6Fu0hDXKA.desc=No Description
betterquesting.quest.uHCMvP2aV_m0RNlKG4Jj2Q.name=Trigger: LV Tier Skip
betterquesting.quest.uHCMvP2aV_m0RNlKG4Jj2Q.desc=No Description
betterquesting.quest.GDgXwpofX9WTCxrBYRc88Q.name=Trigger: MV Tier Skip
betterquesting.quest.GDgXwpofX9WTCxrBYRc88Q.desc=No Description
betterquesting.quest.HDvCr0RvVvu2QvKev1mvOg.name=Trigger: ZPM Tier Skip
betterquesting.quest.HDvCr0RvVvu2QvKev1mvOg.desc=No Description
betterquesting.quest.6WgUfKHLVritlMHwZhD7tA.name=§c§lAmmo and Magazines
betterquesting.quest.6WgUfKHLVritlMHwZhD7tA.desc=Each gun takes one kind of ammunition. Loose rounds (Stone Bullets, 9mm Bullets, Shotgun Shells, Rifle Bullets) go straight into guns such as the Hand Cannon, Revolver, Sawed Off and Bolt Action Rifle. Pistols, SMGs and assault rifles take magazines, which are filled from loose rounds.%n%nHold any round or a loaded magazine to complete this quest. Stone Bullets are the easy ones: three cobblestone, a gunpowder and a bronze nugget at a crafting table make sixteen.%n%nSneak and right-click a magazine to empty it back into loose rounds and an empty magazine, so nothing you press is ever wasted.%n%n[note]Ammo is the real cost of a gun. The Ammo Logistics chapter shows how to build a proper production line.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.edcduXKkVtWx2j1rZqdF-w.name=§c§lFire, Reload, Zoom
betterquesting.quest.edcduXKkVtWx2j1rZqdF-w.desc=Every gun here uses the same three controls. Hold left click to fire (hold it down on automatic guns), press the Reload key (R by default) to put in fresh ammunition, and right-click to zoom on guns that have a scope. Rebind the keys under GregGuns in the Controls menu.%n%nThis quest wants any one of the early guns in your inventory: the Hand Cannon from the Steam chapter, or a 9mm Pistol, Revolver, Sawed Off or Bolt Action Rifle from LV. If you have not built one yet, pick a path and come back, or open the Steam chapter and craft the Hand Cannon first.%n%nReloading puts a short lockout on the gun, and each gun has its own reload time. Press Reload before the fight, not in the middle of it.%n%n[note]Hold a gun and read its tooltip: the ammo it takes, the rounds loaded and its damage. Hold Shift for clip size, range and reload time.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.ys8eY6RtV8iTwNNw6IVUOA.name=§c§lWhere Gear Comes From
betterquesting.quest.ys8eY6RtV8iTwNNw6IVUOA.desc=Nothing here appears from thin air. Guns are assembled from parts, and the parts come from the same GregTech materials as everything else you build. Besides crafting, you can find gear in quest loot bags, in chests at ruins and bunkers, and on hostile soldiers. NEI lists every recipe and drop.%n%nStart with the two simplest parts. A Stone Barrel is stone around a tiny bronze pipe, worked with a file and a hammer. A Wooden Stock is three logs and a saw. Hold both to finish this quest, and the Hand Cannon is one crafting grid away.%n%n[note]Press R on any item in NEI to see how it is made, or U to see what it is used for.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.W8qR4fyDX_aDk-g-tcevbw.name=§c§lReading a Tier
betterquesting.quest.W8qR4fyDX_aDk-g-tcevbw.desc=Every item has a tier, and the tier tells you what it takes. A tier is a machine voltage plus a gate material: Steam is bronze, LV is steel, MV is aluminum, HV is stainless steel, EV is titanium, IV is tungstensteel, and so on up the GregTech ladder. NEI shows the machine and voltage of every recipe, so you can read the tier there.%n%nSo an LV recipe needs an LV machine and steel, an MV recipe needs an MV machine and aluminum, and a machine of a lower tier cannot run it at all. Higher machines can run lower recipes, and they run them faster.%n%nBronze plates are the Steam gate. Hold four to complete this quest and you are ready for the first chapter.%n%n[note]If a recipe in NEI shows a plate you cannot make yet, you are one tier early.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.NW0ZimUpUzOLzQ6eAO4Nvg.name=§c§lWelcome to GregGuns
betterquesting.quest.NW0ZimUpUzOLzQ6eAO4Nvg.desc=GregGuns is a gun and armor line that grows with your GregTech progression instead of sitting beside it. Every weapon here is built in the machines you already know, from a hand-crafted bronze Hand Cannon at the start to missiles that cross the map at the end.%n%nThe chapters climb the tiers in order: Steam, LV, MV, HV, EV, IV, LuV and ZPM. Each one opens with the gate material of its tier (bronze, steel, aluminum, stainless steel, titanium, tungstensteel and onward), adds a few guns and a set of armor, and asks you to build the ammunition for them. Side chapters cover ammo production, machines, gear, structures, mobs and the ICBM module, so you can wander off the main path whenever you like.%n%nYou do not have to read everything. Start with the four quests next to this one: they cover controls, ammo, parts and tiers, and each asks you to hold something real. Then follow the thick lines into the Steam chapter and build your first gun.%n%n[note]This is the only quest that asks you to check a box. Everything after it wants something you built, found or killed.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.97ByAsUoUs6TYUKXeYpGHw.name=§c§lFirst Blood
betterquesting.quest.97ByAsUoUs6TYUKXeYpGHw.desc=Zombies come out at night, and a Hand Cannon is a fine answer. Kill five of them. Stand your ground, shoot, then step back and reload before they close the gap. One round per shot means each one has to count.%n%n[note]Zombies drop rotten flesh and sometimes better things. Keep your bullets stocked.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.eQ7hWE3jV5y_EliMziLpsw.name=§c§lHand Cannon
betterquesting.quest.eQ7hWE3jV5y_EliMziLpsw.desc=A bronze and wood muzzle-loader for people who do not own a single wire yet. The Hand Cannon fires one Stone Bullet per shot and must be reloaded after every one, so it is slow and loud, but it needs no power and no machine.%n%nIt is crafted at a crafting table from a Stone Barrel, a Wooden Stock, flint and steel and a bronze plate, with a hard hammer in the grid. The Gear quest on the start page covered the barrel and stock; check NEI for the exact layout.%n%n[note]The ball falls in a slight arc over distance, so aim a little high at long range. A reload takes about a second and a half.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.Id6LqXtlVYKNNi_Lh3NZuQ.name=§c§lSteam-Age Arms
betterquesting.quest.Id6LqXtlVYKNNi_Lh3NZuQ.desc=Before electricity, there is bronze. The Steam chapter builds everything with a crafting table, a hammer and a file: a single-shot Hand Cannon, stone ammunition, and three sets of light armor. No machine is required, although one steam-powered Ammo Press makes bullets for you.%n%nThe gate material here is bronze (cast iron for the Miner set). Hold eight bronze plates to open the chapter; the Hand Cannon eats a plate, and the Steam armor takes fourteen.%n%nThe plan is simple. Build the cannon and some bullets, test them on zombies, then dress for the job: Tanned Leather is the base of every armor set, and bronze plates armor the parts that matter. When you have all of that and a few steel plates, the LV chapter is next.%n%n[note]This chapter pays the first loot bags and Pam's snacks. Eat up, then go shoot something.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.TCrRly4gVIaC56th9bwd2w.name=§c§lT1 Miner Armor
betterquesting.quest.TCrRly4gVIaC56th9bwd2w.desc=The Miner set trades some of the Scout's lightness for cast iron plates and a helmet with a yellow band. The Miner's Jacket is the quest item: six Tanned Leather above two cast iron plates, crafted by hand. Cast iron comes from the Better Than Iron quests, and its plates are hammered flat from ingots.%n%nAll four pieces are crafted at a table; NEI shows each pattern. The helmet wants yellow dye, and the boots use cast iron nuggets.%n%n[note]Cast iron is the alternative gate for the Steam tier. If you have bronze but no cast iron yet, build the Scout set first.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.DhGoGNiAWI-UXZrxxpGL6Q.name=§c§lT1 Scout Armor
betterquesting.quest.DhGoGNiAWI-UXZrxxpGL6Q.desc=The Bandit set is the lightest armor in the tab: plain leather with a little Tanned Leather, held together with a few bronze plates. Each piece adds to your armor value, and none of them needs a machine. The Bandit Vest is the quest item: two Tanned Leather, six leather and a bronze plate in a crafting grid. Check NEI for the pattern of each piece: mask, vest, pants and boots.%n%nTier 1 armor will not stop much damage, but it costs little and keeps you in the fight until you can afford steel. Each piece comes in several camo patterns, and the Camo Bench cycles them later.%n%n[note]Build a full set if you can: the armor values add up.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.wSQq38uvXRekExzXdeLFhg.name=§c§lSteam Ammo Press
betterquesting.quest.wSQq38uvXRekExzXdeLFhg.desc=The Steam Ammo Press is your first GregGuns machine. It runs on steam like GregTech's other bronze machines and presses ammunition from loose parts, so you can load a stack of cobblestone and walk away. One run makes twenty-four Stone Bullets, eight more than hand crafting.%n%nIts recipe is hand-crafted: three small bronze pipes, two pistons, a bronze hull and three bronze plates. Feed it steam from any side except the front; it vents steam out of the front after every run.%n%nA steam press can run any Ammo Press recipe up to LV, only at half the speed of an electric machine. That means you can start making 9mm bullets before you have a single volt, if you have the brass and lead.%n%n[note]The press has its own recipe tab in NEI. Check it for every recipe it runs.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.gJogZbB0WC-PHZhE1XBtjg.name=§c§lStone Bullets
betterquesting.quest.gJogZbB0WC-PHZhE1XBtjg.desc=The Hand Cannon eats one Stone Bullet per shot, so you will want a lot of them. At a crafting table, three cobblestone, a gunpowder and a bronze nugget make sixteen bullets. Hold thirty-two to finish the quest.%n%nGunpowder drops from creepers, and GregTech can mix it too. Bronze nuggets are made from bronze ingots. If you would rather not hand-craft, the next quest builds a steam machine that does it for you.%n%n[note]Stone Bullets are Steam-tier ammo. Rounds for the LV guns are made in the Ammo Press from brass foil, lead or steel rounds, and gunpowder.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.WPoszcLHWoKl99iKsgqbdg.name=§c§lSteam Age Done
betterquesting.quest.WPoszcLHWoKl99iKsgqbdg.desc=You have a cannon, bullets, a press and armor, and the zombies are learning to fear you. Steam is done. The next gate is steel, and steel is a GregTech project: make it in your furnace setup, press it into plates, and the LV chapter opens.%n%nLV changes the game. The Hand Cannon gives way to magazine-fed pistols, a revolver, a scoped rifle and a shotgun; armor moves up to steel; and ammo becomes a production line with its own machine. All of it is on the next tab to the right of this one.%n%nHold four steel plates to finish the chapter. Use the loot bags to patch any gaps in your kit, and eat something.%n%n[note]You do not need to finish every quest here to open LV. The LV chapter opens from the pack's own tier quests.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.hb2nDLwyUgWeBRV41k_0Bw.name=§c§lTanned Leather
betterquesting.quest.hb2nDLwyUgWeBRV41k_0Bw.desc=Tanned Leather is the lining of almost every armor set in GregGuns, from the Steam age to the late game. It is the pack's own material, the same one your first backpack takes. Bind four leather with four string and a Woven Cotton into Bound Leather, then hang it on a Tinkers' drying rack for about ten minutes.%n%nYou need plenty: the Steam armor alone takes eleven, so keep a few racks busy. Hold four to finish this quest. Once you have an LV Chemical Bath, two leather in phosphoric acid make one with no wait. NEI shows both recipes.%n%n[note]The Stone Age quest of the same name walks you through the drying rack.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.AVQL82mkXP-LB9GnCstKfg.name=§b§lNuclear Power Cell
betterquesting.quest.AVQL82mkXP-LB9GnCstKfg.desc=A sealed uranium cell, the power core of the Nuclear Death Ray. One cell goes into the Death Ray's recipe; the gun itself runs on stored energy and never burns cells as ammo. The cell is a ZPM Assembly Line craft that puts your lead, redstone and enriched uranium to work.%n%nOne cell comes from two Naquadah alloy plates, two lead plates, four enriched uranium dust, two redstone dust, a ZPM circuit and soldering alloy. The research item is Power Plating.%n%n[warn]The cell is radioactive. Carry it only in full radiation hazmat, or keep it in a chest until the Death Ray craft.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.kKAhLTGpU9OkSP5mpAQ9xw.name=§b§lNuclear Death Ray
betterquesting.quest.kKAhLTGpU9OkSP5mpAQ9xw.desc=The best energy weapon in the tree. Hold the trigger and it fires a continuous beam that does heavy damage every tick and ignores armor. It has no reload. When the charge is gone, it is gone.%n%nIt is an Assembly Line recipe, researched from the Alien Blaster. The inputs are a Rad Emitter, a Nuclear Power Cell, a Carbon Receiver and Gunstock, a LuV field generator, two ZPM circuits, four lead plates, four Naquadah alloy plates and eight screws, with 1,152 mB of soldering alloy and 500 mB of lubricant. NEI has the exact list.%n%nIt is a tier 7 electric item holding 10 billion EU, and a beam tick costs 20 million EU. Charge it only in a ZPM charger or battery buffer; a lower one will not accept it.%n%n[note]The lead in the recipe is the shielding. Keep a spare Alien Blaster before you start, or the scan has nothing to read.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.GqpwePIVV6GeDRh-yMkzkw.name=§b§lNuclear Arms
betterquesting.quest.GqpwePIVV6GeDRh-yMkzkw.desc=The top of the GregGuns tree. ZPM brings the Nuclear Death Ray, the Nuke Launcher and the components behind them, and every one is an Assembly Line build. Naquadah alloy is the gate, so the first thing you need is a supply of its plates.%n%nZPM weapons run at 122,880 EU/t recipes with lead shielding, ZPM circuits, soldering alloy and lubricant, and research items you scanned yourself. The Death Ray is a tier 7 electric item that charges only in a ZPM charger or battery buffer. The Nuke Launcher is ammo-fed.%n%nThis tier handles uranium. The tactical nuke rocket, the Nuclear Power Cell, the Small Nuclear Warhead and the Rad Emitter are radioactive, and GT irradiates anyone who carries them without full radiation hazmat. Plan your storage before you build.%n%n[note]Press R over any item in NEI for its recipe. Quests only check what you carry and never take it.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.tUMCQKVHVRarlhC600tDTQ.name=§b§lNuke Launcher
betterquesting.quest.tUMCQKVHVRarlhC600tDTQ.desc=A shoulder-fired nuclear weapon. Inside 60%% of its blast radius it annihilates anything that lives, and a boss takes half of its maximum health.%n%nIt is an Assembly Line build, researched from the Grim Reaper. The inputs are two Hardened Steel Barrels, a Carbon Receiver, a ZPM electric motor, two ZPM circuits, four lead plates, four Naquadah alloy plates and eight screws, with soldering alloy and lubricant. The tactical nuke rocket is its ammo.%n%n[warn]The nuke is the largest blast of any GregGuns gun. Do not fire it from inside your own base.[/warn]%n%n[note]Servers that keep explosions.blockDamage off leave the terrain intact. Creatures are still hit.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.T18BX594XP2ljkhiBXBqog.name=§b§lTactical Nuke Rocket
betterquesting.quest.T18BX594XP2ljkhiBXBqog.desc=A rocket with a nuclear warhead. One is enough to level a neighborhood, so treat it like a decision.%n%nBuild it in the ZPM Assembly Line from a regular Rocket, a Small Nuclear Warhead, two Naquadah alloy plates, two lead plates, a ZPM circuit and soldering alloy. The research item is a Rocket.%n%n[warn]Radioactive, and it is the biggest blast any GregGuns gun fires. Only fire it where nobody lives, and wear full radiation hazmat while you carry it.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest._6gjS8_UX6OQ_71dO6mvdg.name=§b§lRad Emitter
betterquesting.quest._6gjS8_UX6OQ_71dO6mvdg.desc=The Rad Emitter is the Death Ray's business end: a ZPM emitter that sprays radiation along a beam. It is a ZPM Assembly Line part.%n%nBuild it from a ZPM emitter, two lead plates, one enriched uranium dust, two Mechanical Parts T3, two ZPM circuits and soldering alloy. The research item is a Sonic Emitter, scanned in a Research Station. NEI shows the full recipe.%n%n[warn]The emitter is radioactive. Carry it only in full radiation hazmat.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest._WK5gkzGU72JerH0PueN0g.name=§b§lTop of the Tree
betterquesting.quest._WK5gkzGU72JerH0PueN0g.desc=That is the top of the GregGuns gun tree. A continuous beam that ignores armor, and a rocket launcher that ends arguments. You built both from naquadah, lead and uranium, on the same Assembly Line that makes the rest of the pack's ZPM gear.%n%nFrom here, the rest of the mod is yours to play with. The ICBM line takes you from rockets to missiles and silos, the NPC chapters have things worth hunting, and the pack has plenty of ZPM to go. Take the coins, open the bags, and keep your hazmat on.%n%nIf you want a longer game, go back and fill in the quests you skipped. Every chapter has side builds that pay well and teach something the capstones do not.%n%n[note]This capstone pays out the biggest reward in the tab, with four bags and the best meal.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.f-_Hf21OVQONGJCf-zeuyg.name=§b§lSmall Nuclear Warhead
betterquesting.quest.f-_Hf21OVQONGJCf-zeuyg.desc=The warhead is the payload of a tactical nuke rocket. It is a lead-shielded block of uranium and TNT wired to a proximity fuze.%n%nCraft two at a time in a ZPM Assembly Line from lead plates, TNT, LuV circuits, enriched uranium dust and one Naquadah alloy plate, with soldering alloy. NEI lists the research item and the rest.%n%n[warn]The warhead is radioactive, and so is the tactical nuke rocket you build from it. Carry them only in full radiation hazmat.[/warn]
# END questbook

