gregguns.fallout.tip.earth=Radioactive ground left by a nuclear blast. Standing on it irradiates you unless you wear hazmat armor.
gregguns.fallout.tip.earth.1=Fades back to ordinary ground over time, but never while fallout goo stands in its chunk.
gregguns.fallout.tip.earth.2=Its rubble goes in a Centrifuge for lead, thorium and uranium.
gregguns.fallout.tip.hot_earth=Hot irradiated ground from the inner fallout of a ZPM or better blast. Standing on it irradiates you unless you wear hazmat armor.
gregguns.fallout.tip.hot_earth.1=Fades back to ordinary ground over time, but never while fallout goo stands in its chunk.
gregguns.fallout.tip.hot_earth.2=Its hot rubble gives a trace of fissile material in a Centrifuge, far less than the warhead used.
gregguns.fallout.tip.rubble=Radioactive. Carrying it irradiates you unless you wear hazmat armor.
gregguns.fallout.tip.rubble.1=Centrifuge (HV): lead, thorium and uranium dust.
gregguns.fallout.tip.rubble.2=Has no recycling value of its own, so it is never free fuel.
gregguns.fallout.tip.hot_rubble=Hot and radioactive. Carrying it irradiates you harder than plain rubble, unless you wear hazmat armor.
gregguns.fallout.tip.hot_rubble.1=Centrifuge (HV): lead, thorium and uranium, with a small chance of uranium-235 and plutonium.
gregguns.fallout.tip.hot_rubble.2=A whole blast returns at most a quarter of its warhead's core.
gregguns.fallout.tip.trinitite=Glassy rock fused by the heat of a ZPM or better blast, found near ground zero.
gregguns.fallout.tip.trinitite.1=Breaks into a Trinitite Shard.
gregguns.fallout.tip.shard=A sliver of trinitite. Radioactive: carrying it irradiates you unless you wear hazmat armor.
gregguns.fallout.tip.shard.1=Macerator: Crushed Trinitite.
gregguns.fallout.tip.crushed=Macerated trinitite. Radioactive: carrying it irradiates you unless you wear hazmat armor.
gregguns.fallout.tip.crushed.1=Centrifuge (HV): uranium and thorium, with a trace of plutonium and uranium-235.
gregguns.fallout.tip.goo_block=Rare, near ground zero. While it stands, the irradiated earth in its chunk does not fade. Dig it up to let the land recover.
gregguns.fallout.tip.goo_block.1=Breaks into Fallout Goo. Mine it with a shovel.
gregguns.fallout.tip.hot_goo_block=Rare goo from a ZPM or better blast. While it stands, the irradiated earth in its chunk does not fade. Dig it up to let the land recover.
gregguns.fallout.tip.hot_goo_block.1=Breaks into Hot Fallout Goo. Mine it with a shovel.
gregguns.fallout.tip.goo=Radioactive sludge of fission products. Carrying it irradiates you unless you wear hazmat armor.
gregguns.fallout.tip.goo.1=Chemical Reactor (LuV) with nitric acid: Dissolved Fallout Goo.
gregguns.fallout.tip.hot_goo=Hot radioactive sludge from a ZPM or better blast. Carrying it irradiates you harder, unless you wear hazmat armor.
gregguns.fallout.tip.hot_goo.1=Chemical Reactor (LuV) with nitric acid: Dissolved Hot Fallout Goo.
gregguns.fallout.tip.dissolved=Fallout goo in acid. Still radioactive.
gregguns.fallout.tip.dissolved.1=Centrifuge (EV): technetium, promethium, neptunium, plutonium-241, americium and curium, with krypton and xenon.
gregguns.fallout.tip.dissolved_hot=Hot fallout goo in acid. Still radioactive.
gregguns.fallout.tip.dissolved_hot.1=Centrifuge (EV): neptunium, plutonium-241, americium, curium, and traces of californium and fermium, with krypton and xenon.

